  "4.748.0" => "Fairy Effects",
  "4.749.0" => "Smaller Magic Circles",
  "4.750.0" => "Adventure Mode",
  "4.751.0" => "Battle Evaluations",
  "4.752.0" => "Progressing in Adventure Mode",
  "4.753.0" => "Victory Rewards",
  "4.754.0" => "Restriction Icons",
  "4.755.0" => "Item Cards",
  "4.756.0" => "Treasure Icons",
  "4.757.0" => "Search Screen",
  "4.758.0" => "Battle-Information Screen",
  "4.759.0" => "Materials",
  "4.760.0" => "Dropped Weapons",
  "4.761.0" => "Weapon Information",
  "4.762.0" => "Leveling Up",
  "4.763.0" => "Rupees",
  "4.764.0" => "Heart Containers",
  "4.765.0" => "Gold Skulltulas",
  "4.766.0" => "Illustration Pieces",
  "4.767.0" => "Badge Market",
  "4.768.0" => "Training Dojo",
  "4.769.0" => "Apothecary",
  "4.770.0" => "Fusing Weapons",
  "4.771.0" => "Select Scenario Screen",
  "4.772.0" => "Adventure Mode Difficulty",
  "4.773.0" => "Network Links",
  "4.774.0" => "Friend Bonus",
  "4.775.0" => "Boss Keys",
  "4.776.0" => "Defeating enemies fills your A6Special Attack gaugeR.

Press Pe to use up your Special Attack gauge and
perform a powerful A6Special AttackR.",
  "4.777.0" => "Alternatively, if your Special Move gauge is full,
press and hold A to use up the entire gauge to
perform a Crippling Strike.",
  "4.778.0" => "Connecting with a Crippling Strike on a strong
enemy will force it to the ground where it will
be left open to a Weak Point Smash.",
  "4.779.0" => "Press Pl when your Magic gauge is full to
use the A6Focus SpiritR ability.",
  "4.780.0" => "While Focus Spirit is active, attack power and
speed increase, incoming knock-back damage
is reduced, and defeating a certain number of
enemies will yield various A6special bonusesR.",
  "4.781.0" => "Press Pe while under the effects of Focus Spirit
to completely consume your Magic gauge, allowing
you to use a A6Focus Spirit AttackR that knocks your
opponents down, exposing their Weak Points.",
  "4.782.0" => "Enemies sometimes expose weak points
during specific attacks. A A6Weak Point gaugeR
will appear above an enemy's head when it's
vulnerable to a counterattack.",
  "4.783.0" => "Attack quickly and brutally whenever you see
the Weak Point gauge in order to chip it away.",
  "4.784.0" => "Once the gauge is completely reduced, you'll be
able to perform a powerful A6Weak Point SmashR.",
  "4.785.0" => "By pressing Pf (or the ZL Button on the New
Nintendo 3DS and New Nintendo 3DS XL), you can
make the camera lock on to a nearby powerful
enemy.",
  "4.786.0" => "On New Nintendo 3DS and New Nintendo 3DS XL
systems, you can move PK (the C Stick)
while A6targetingR an enemy to
change the enemy being targeted.",
  "4.787.0" => "Press Pd to evade enemy attacks.",
  "4.788.0" => "Hold Pg to guard against enemy attacks.",
  "4.789.0" => "Hitting an enemy with a fire elemental attack
will cause the enemy to blow up when it hits
the ground, causing additional damage to
enemies caught in the blast.",
  "4.790.0" => "Hitting an enemy with a water elemental attack
will cause the enemy to continue taking damage
over a set period of time.",
  "4.791.0" => "Enemies sent flying by lightning elemental attacks
will take extra damage from your attacks while in
the air.",
  "4.792.0" => "Light elemental attacks gradually become
stronger as you unleash continuous attacks
on groups of enemies.",
  "4.793.0" => "Darkness elemental attacks gradually become
stronger as you unleash a continuous attack
on a single enemy.",
  "4.794.0" => "Pick up A6Magic JarsR to refill your A6Magic gaugeR.
When your Magic gauge is full, you can use
a technique called A6Focus SpiritR.",
  "4.795.0" => "When your Magic gauge is full, you can use
Unleash Magic.",
  "4.796.0" => "Seize keeps to stem the flow of enemy
reinforcements. To take a keep, fully reduce
its Keep Meter by defeating enough enemies
within the keep.",
  "4.797.0" => "The Keep Meter can be found below the
battlefield map. Once the Keep Meter
is empty, the A6Keep BossR will appear.
Defeat him and the keep is yours!",
  "4.798.0" => "Once the Keep Meter is depleted, a Keep
Commander appears. Defeat the commander
and the keep is yours.",
  "4.799.0" => "Outposts continue to spawn soldiers
for the side that controls them.",
  "4.800.0" => "Defeating an A6Outpost CaptainR captures that
outpost for your forces. However, if an Allied
Captain at an outpost is defeated, then the
enemy forces will claim that outpost instead.",
  "4.801.0" => "Conversely, if the captain guarding an allied
outpost falls, the enemy will gain control of it.",
  "4.802.0" => "Each army has a A6morale levelR. When morale
is high, an army will glow brightly and become
stronger. When morale is low, the army will
look darkly shaded instead.",
  "4.803.0" => "The army's battle ability increases when morale
is high and weakens when morale low.",
  "4.804.0" => "Injured allies can be aided by coming into
contact with the A6rescue areaR surrounding
them.",
  "4.805.0" => "A6RescuingR an injured ally will restore that
warrior's health.",
  "4.806.0" => "By acquiring item power-ups on the battlefield,
you can gain the ability to use stronger versions
of items for a short amount of time.",
  "4.807.0" => "Giant Bosses possess health and strength far
surpassing those of normal foes. Find items
that attack the monster's weak points and
set yourself up for a Weak Point Smash!",
  "4.808.0" => "Each Giant Boss has a weakness to one specific
item. If you manage to properly target a giant
boss' weakness, you can create a chance for
yourself to pull of a Weak Point Smash.",
  "4.809.0" => "A6SummonersR are capable of spawning new units.
They will continue spawning units until they
are defeated, so make their defeat a priority!",
  "4.810.0" => "Summoners will continue spawning units until they
are defeated, so make their defeat a priority!",
  "4.811.0" => "Damage areas are hazard zones where your allies'
health will continue to decrease just by remaining
in the affected area.",
  "4.812.0" => "Clearing up damage areas is the key to moving
forward and keeping allies safe.",
  "4.813.0" => "Some enemies have the ability to directly damage
allied keeps.",
  "4.814.0" => "Left unchecked, these attacks can level keeps or
even bases, so don't let an enemy continue
directly attacking a keep!",
  "4.815.0" => "Activating a A6Magic CircleR will aid your
allies with A6powerful magicR and give your forces
an advantage in battle.",
  "4.816.0" => "Stand on a glowing magic circle and press the
button that is displayed on screen to activate it.
",
  "4.817.0" => "A6BombsR can destroy certain boulders or walls.
Doing so will often open new routes or even
uncover useful items.",
  "4.818.0" => "Breaking rocks will often open new routes or
uncover useful items.",
  "4.819.0" => "Deku Babas attack by spewing poison. A6They cannotR
A6be defeated by normal attacksR, so you must find
some other method of inflicting damage.",
  "4.820.0" => "Deku Babas cannot be defeated by normal attacks,
so you must find some other method of inflicting
damage.",
  "4.821.0" => "If you don't find some way to remove a Wall
of Vines, you won't be able to proceed. A6VinesR
A6cannot be cut by normal attacksR, so you must
find another way to hack through them.",
  "4.822.0" => "Vines cannot be cut by normal attacks, so you
must find another way to hack through them.",
  "4.823.0" => "Stone statues called A6BeamosR attack with powerful
beams once they spot you.",
  "4.824.0" => "Beamos are extraordinarily tough, A6so normalR
A6attacks will be ineffectiveR. Find some means
of attacking Beamos!",
  "4.825.0" => "Make sure to defend your allies! Ensuring they
reach their destinations safely is very important!
If an ally is attacked by enemies to the point of
having to flee, you could very well lose a battle!",
  "4.826.0" => "If an ally is attacked by enemies to the point of
having to flee, you could very well lose a battle!",
  "4.827.0" => "The A6Turncoat LeaderR within your ranks
will slowly convert allied units into enemies.
If you discover and defeat the Turncoat Leader,
all the soldiers who've already defected will flee.",
  "4.828.0" => "If you discover and defeat a traitorous engineer,
all the soldiers who've already defected will flee.",
  "4.829.0" => "Midna draws great power from the A6TwilightR
A6RealmR keeps scattered across the battlefield.
A6Capture those keepsR to return her to normal.",
  "4.830.0" => "By capturing keeps, you can return each Twilight
Realm zone to normal, which will reduce Midna's
strength.",
  "4.831.0" => "To halt The Imprisoned's advance, you need to
use A6the GroosenatorR.",
  "4.832.0" => "A6After capturing a keepR, get close to the
Groosenator and press the button that is displayed
on screen to use it.
",
  "4.833.0" => "Magic Keeps combine the A6energies of a group ofR
A6keepsR to weave powerful enhancements, causing
strong enemies to spawn. A6Breaking this connectionR
stops the flow of stronger-than-normal monsters.",
  "4.834.0" => "If you manage to break the chain of a linked keep,
the enemy troops will lose their enhancements.",
  "4.835.0" => "A great power resides in the A6Light ArrowsR.
However, that power is easily suppressed by
Magic Sealer Troops. Bring back the power by
defeating the troops in question!",
  "4.836.0" => "The more power you manage to bring back to the
arrows, the stronger an effect they will have on
A6Ganon's movementsR!",
  "4.837.0" => "While inside A6keeps with barriersR,
your warrior and your warrior's allies
will continually take damage.",
  "4.838.0" => "To avoid this, you will have to rescue the
A6elemental fairyR by A6capturing the keepR it's
trapped inside. This fairy will help you once
it's freed.",
  "4.839.0" => "Using A6fairies of the same element as the keepR
will neutralize the barrier there and prevent you
from taking damage.",
  "4.840.0" => "Use the Touch Screen or P5 to select
the fairy, and then press Pi to use it.",
  "4.841.0" => "There are also some rare fairies that, instead
of bestowing elemental properties, give you
special bonuses.",
  "4.842.0" => "If you activate a A6Magic CircleR, A6powerful magicR
will help your allies and give your forces an
advantage. Stand on a glowing Magic Circle
and press Pb to use it.",
  "4.843.0" => "After capturing a keep with a Magic Circle in
it, stand in the center of the Magic Circle and
press A to activate it.",
  "4.844.0" => "In Adventure Mode, your goal is to access
new areas of the map by winning battles
with various special rules. Ultimately, you
must find and defeat the A6Dark RulerR.",
  "4.845.0" => "Where your character can move on the world
map depends on the A6battle rankR you have
attained in the battles on each map square.
Higher ranks give you more options!",
  "4.846.0" => "In Adventure Mode, certain maps carry A6special
rewardsR you can get if you win battles on them.
Map squares with a special reward will show an
icon representing the reward.",
  "4.847.0" => "Some battles will restrict A6which weapons orR
A6warriors can be usedR. Make sure to keep all
your warriors trained and ready to fight!",
  "4.848.0" => "By using A6Item CardsR on the Adventure Mode
Search screen, you may unlock hidden
objects and other secrets.",
  "4.849.0" => "You can gain Item Cards by winning battles
marked with Item Card icons, such as the
Compass or Bombs.",
  "4.850.0" => "Item Card icons will continue to appear
as you win more battles.",
  "4.851.0" => "Pieces of Heart, Heart Containers, and Skulltulas
are all hidden in various places around battlefields,
and can be acquired by winning battles during
which you've found them.",
  "4.852.0" => "Use A6Item CardsR to discover hidden things
on the Adventure Mode Search screen.",
  "4.853.0" => "Select the Item Card you want to use from
the list, and then choose the square you want
to investigate on the map. A6If the square andR
A6card match, you've made a successful searchR!",
  "4.854.0" => "If your investigation succeeds, you may uncover
a new route or powerful weapon, A6though youR
A6can only acquire them by meeting the battle-R
A6rank requirements of that missionR.",
  "4.855.0" => "The Adventure Mode battle-info screen
allows you to check details about the battle,
including what sorts of rewards are at stake.",
  "4.856.0" => "By gathering materials, you can create badges in
the Badge Market or mixtures in the Apothecary.",
  "4.857.0" => "The types of material you collect depend on the
types of enemies you defeat. Captains might
drop bronze or silver ingredients, while bosses
sometimes drop silver or gold ingredients.",
  "4.858.0" => "If you pick up a weapon mid-battle, you will
be able to use that weapon once you have
claimed victory in that battle.",
  "4.859.0" => "The weapons you find vary in attack strength
and elemental skills, so make sure to check the
attributes and equip a weapon that will be the
most useful for a particular mission.",
  "4.860.0" => "After choosing a warrior, you will need to choose
which weapon to wield (assuming you have
found additional weapons).",
  "4.861.0" => "A6Attack StrengthR:
The higher the value, the more damage you deal
to enemies. The value is decided based on A6basicR
A6weapon strengthR and the weapon's A6star ratingR.",
  "4.862.0" => "A6SkillR:
Skills attached to weapons give them various
added effects. If a skill is sealed, you must
defeat a certain number of foes to unlock it.",
  "4.863.0" => "A6ElementR:
Equipping the right element for the right enemy
or battle can make all the difference.",
  "4.864.0" => "Leveling up A6increases a warrior's basic attackR
A6strength and maximum healthR.",
  "4.865.0" => "Your warrior's A6experience gaugeR will go up
as you defeat enemies. When the gauge is full,
the warrior levels up.",
  "4.866.0" => "You can spend Rupees in the various shops
in the Bazaar.",
  "4.867.0" => "Rupees are the currency of Hyrule. They are
collected automatically shortly after they appear.
Find Rupees by defeating enemies and smashing
jars.",
  "4.868.0" => "A6Heart ContainerR:
Restores all of your health and increases
your maximum health by one heart.",
  "4.869.0" => "A6Piece of HeartR:
Restores all of your health. Collect four of these
to make a new Heart Container and increase
your maximum health by one heart.",
  "4.870.0" => "You can check information on Heart Containers
and Pieces of Heart hidden on a given battlefield
from the Select Scenario screen. However, they
only appear when using the specified warrior.",
  "4.871.0" => "There are A6180 Gold SkulltulasR hidden around
the world. By defeating them and gathering
the illustration pieces they drop, you will be
rewarded with certain A6perksR.",
  "4.872.0" => "Gold Skulltulas will only appear A6within theR
A6spider's webR on the map once you fulfill
certain battle conditions. They flee after a set
period of time has passed, so move quickly!",
  "4.873.0" => "You can check information on Gold Skulltulas
hidden on a given battlefield from the Select
Scenario screen. However, some only appear
when using specific warriors or weapons.",
  "4.874.0" => "By collecting the pieces and completing
illustrations, you can get your hands on
certain A6rewardsR. To earn new illustration
pieces, defeat Gold Skulltulas!",
  "4.875.0" => "You will get one illustration piece for every
Gold Skulltula you defeat.",
  "4.876.0" => "Creating badges for your warriors at the Badge
Market will help improve their battle abilities.
The bonuses granted by a badge apply only
A6to the warrior for whom it was createdR.",
  "4.877.0" => "Creating badges requires both A6RupeesR and
specific A6materialsR, but the benefits they add
to warriors can be immensely helpful in battle.",
  "4.878.0" => "You can spend Rupees at the Training Dojo to
help warriors level up. However, A6you will not beR
A6able to raise their level beyond the level of theR
A6current highest-level warriorR.",
  "4.879.0" => "The higher the warrior's level, the more Rupees
it will cost to train the warrior. It's more useful to
use the Training Dojo to grow low-level warriors.",
  "4.880.0" => "Visit the Apothecary to create a A6mixtureR for
the next battle. The effects can be powerful, but
very temporary.",
  "4.881.0" => "Furthermore, for warriors who've crafted an
A6Empty Bottle badgeR, the Apothecary will
provide restorative A6potionsR for every battle,
free of charge!",
  "4.882.0" => "A6As you defeat more Gold SkulltulasR, you will
be able to create more varieties of mixtures
and stock up on more types of potion.
Plus, their effects will become stronger!",
  "4.883.0" => "By fusing weapons, you can transfer A6skillsR
between A6weapons you ownR.",
  "4.884.0" => "To transfer a skill, you will need to spend an
amount of A6RupeesR based on the A6source weaponR
and the type of skill. The source weapon will also
be destroyed in the process.",
  "4.885.0" => "You can only add skills to weapons with empty
skill slots. Overwriting previously-activated skills
and moving sealed skills won't work.",
  "4.886.0" => "You can check information on heart containers
and Gold Skulltulas that remain hidden on a
given battlefield from the Select Scenario screen.",
  "4.887.0" => "Do you see a Heart Container or Gold Skulltula
in the stage information? If you play with the
warrior or weapon shown next to them, those
items may appear!",
  "4.888.0" => "Warriors with the 'Recommended' mark have
elemental affinity appropriate for the given
battle, meaning they will deal more damage
to the enemies found on that battlefield.",
  "4.889.0" => "Press Pi to use your currently equipped item,
such as A6bombsR or a A6potionR.",
  "4.890.0" => "If you're carrying more than one usable item,
you can switch between them by pressing
left and right on P5 or using the item icon
on the lower right of the Touch Screen.",
  "4.891.0" => "A6The difficulty of Adventure Mode is fixedR and
unaffected by the difficulty level set for Legend
and Free modes.",
  "4.892.0" => "A6Other players using network features mayR 
A6appear on your map as alternate-coloredR
A6LinksR. Winning your battle will help them out!",
  "4.893.0" => "Battles waged on a map with Network Links
are much more difficult, but you're also
awarded more powerful weapons and
other beneficial items.",
  "4.894.0" => "On maps with Network Links from your friends,
you will acquire better rewards.",
  "4.895.0" => "If a friend helps your Link, you will be able
to claim a bonus.",
  "4.896.0" => "If an Enemy Base appears to be locked, it
means a boss has shut it tight. To unlock
the Enemy Base, find a A6Boss KeyR hidden
in a keep.",
  "4.897.0" => "Once you acquire the Boss Key, A6walking nearR
A6the Enemy BaseR will open its gates.",
  "4.898.0" => "Once you've taken the Boss Key out of its
chest, getting near the Enemy Stronghold
with the key in your possession is enough
to unlock its gates.",
  "4.899.0" => "Neutral Keeps",
  "4.900.0" => "Keeps shown in white on the map are considered
A6neutral keepsR as they belong to neither the enemy
nor the allied forces.",
  "4.901.0" => "When the number of soldiers in a neutral keep
goes up, the A6Capture GaugeR also increases.",
  "4.902.0" => "The side that completes the Capture Gauge first
will claim the keep. Defeat enemies and increase
the number of allies in the keep to capture it!",
  "4.903.0" => "An elemental effect can be added to certain
attacks from specific weapons. The effect will
change depending on whether the weapon has
fire, water, lightning, light, or darkness attributes.",
  "4.904.0" => "Raid Captains",
  "4.905.0" => "In Adventure Mode, a A6Raid CaptainR can march
forth from a keep on the battlefield where the
Allied and Enemy Forces meet and will advance
toward the enemy's nearest keep.",
  "4.906.0" => "Once the nearest enemy keep is claimed by
the unit's forces, the A6Raid CaptainR will continue
on from that keep and look for more positions
to take.",
  "4.907.0" => "About battle types...",
  "4.908.0" => "There are two kinds of battles in Adventure Mode.
In a A6Challenge BattleR, your warriors must go solo.
In A6Adventure BattleR, you and an allied army must
defeat a specific enemy together.",
  "4.909.0" => "Darunia, Goron Chief",
  "4.910.0" => "Ruto, Zora Princess",
  "4.911.0" => "Agitha, Princess of the Insect Kingdom",
  "4.912.0" => "Midna, Twilight Princess",
  "4.913.0" => "Fi, Spirit of the Sword",
  "4.914.0" => "Ghirahim, Demon Lord",
  "4.915.0" => "Zant, Usurper King",
  "4.916.0" => "When Cia opened a doorway to the era of the
Hero of Time, a brave warrior stepped through
the portal and added his strength to the current
battle, just as he'd done ages before.",
  "4.917.0" => "As a proud Goron chieftain, Darunia makes his
home in Goron City, located in the heart of the
volcanic Death Mountain. Like all Gorons, his
diet consists entirely of rocks.",
  "4.918.0" => "It's Goron tradition to refer to loved ones and
trusted allies as "brother," an attribute Darunia
has not left behind on his journey through the
ages.",
  "4.919.0" => "When Cia opened a portal to the era of the Hero
of Time, a princess other than Zelda rose up and
decided to aid the Hero, making it the second
time she would answer Hyrule's call for help.",
  "4.920.0" => "As a princess of the Zoras, Ruto is at home
in the water, ruling over Zora's Domain at
the point where the Zora's River flows into
Lake Hylia.",
  "4.921.0" => "While her refined speech may initially convince
enemies and allies alike that she's stuck up and
snobby, her actions as a warrior instantly remind
those on the battlefield why she's so beloved.",
  "4.922.0" => "Of all the allies the Hero would have on his
long journey, few would be as odd as the
self-described princess of the insect kingdom
from the Era of Twilight.",
  "4.923.0" => "Agitha, as legends state, once asked the Hero
of her time to gather the Golden Bugs of the
land for an elaborate party. This obsession
with bugs has carried over into battle.",
  "4.924.0" => "During battle, Agitha will regularly skip around
and collect bugs, and while this may seem out
of place for a war, she will instantly change
your mind when her friends are in danger.",
  "4.925.0" => "Cia made a critical error when she opened a
portal to the Era of Twilight. While a swarm of
monsters joined her cause, the most powerful
and vicious of Twili joined the Hero's.",
  "4.926.0" => "Midna, the Twilight Princess, ruled over the
Twili people with grace and beauty...until a
curse changed her into the wolf-riding imp
that warriors see on the battlefield.",
  "4.927.0" => "She draws strength from the Twilight Realm, able
to channel it through her versatile hair. She wears
a mask called the Fused Shadow and can even
assemble its full might for a single mighty blow.",
  "4.928.0" => "As the portal to the Era of Twilight opened, the
land was once more subjected to the fearsome
Usurper King, the Twili who brought both the
Twilight Realm and Hyrule to their knees.",
  "4.929.0" => "Zant earned his reputation and title when he
stole the throne from Midna, the Twilight
Princess. Immediately after doing so, he cursed
her and set about invading the land of Hyrule.",
  "4.930.0" => "While Zant is usually able to keep his regal
composure, all of his grace and calmness
melts away when he becomes flustered.
This can make him very dangerous indeed.",
  "4.931.0" => "When Cia opened a portal to Skyloft, the fabled
city in the sky, she never intended to gift the
Hero both a weapon and an ally at the same
time, yet this came to pass.",
  "4.932.0" => "Fi, the spirit that inhabits the Goddess Sword,
is an unusual being. Gifted with acute analytical
senses and lengthy battle-related knowledge,
Fi proves herself vital to any conflict.",
  "4.933.0" => "Despite being a sword and a literal weapon,
Fi possesses amazing grace and dancing
ability. Watching her dance in the face of her
enemies is a truly mesmerizing sight to behold.",
  "4.934.0" => "While a spirit inhabiting a sacred sword came
through the portal from Skyloft, so too did a
spirit from a fearsome and demonic sword,
ready to wreak havoc once more.",
  "4.935.0" => "As a Demon Lord, Ghirahim commanded legions
of monsters during a campaign to resurrect his
true master, the Demon King Demise.",
  "4.936.0" => "Being a sword himself, Ghirahim knows the fine
art of swordplay and proves himself a deadly
fencer with added magical powers. He may come
off as soft, but he's truly deadly in combat.",
  "4.937.0" => "Adventure Mode is a A6special modeR in which
you can acquire heart containers and A6powerful
new weaponsR, power up your warriors, and
unlock A6new warriorsR.",
  "4.938.0" => "Item Card Descriptions",
  "4.939.0" => "A6CompassR: Use this while searching to
identify where an Item Card can be used.",
  "4.940.0" => "A6BombR: Use this on walls to uncover
hidden caves.
A6CandleR: Use this on trees to uncover
hidden stairways.",
  "4.941.0" => "A6LadderR: Use this to move across a single
space of water.
A6Power BraceletR: Use this on heavy rocks
or tombstones to uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.942.0" => "A6Water BombR: Use this on submerged
rocks to destroy them.
A6Digging MittsR: Use these on soft earth to
uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.943.0" => "A6Ice ArrowR: Use this on circles of flame
to uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.944.0" => "A6RaftR: Use this on piers to cross to the
opposite shore.
A6HookshotR: Use this on distant targets to
pull yourself to them.",
  "4.945.0" => "A6RecorderR: Use this on a small body of
water to reveal secrets and enemies.",
  "4.946.0" => "A6Win the battleR to claim the bronze-level reward.
To claim the gold-level reward, A6win the battleR
A6with an 'A' RankR.",
  "4.947.0" => "To find and claim the rewards hidden on various
map squares, A6first uncover them by searching,R
A6and then win the battle on that square to acquireR
A6themR.",
  "4.948.0" => "There are nine illustrations in total. You can
check how many pieces of each illustration
you've gathered by going to the Gallery's
View Illustration section.",
  "4.949.0" => "Try to find them!",
  "4.950.0" => "Try A6searchingR by pressing P2, and then use
an item like the Candle to uncover secrets.",
  "4.951.0" => "Try looking again!",
  "4.952.0" => "Too bad! An A6Item CardR cannot be used here!",
  "4.953.0" => "Here, take one more A6CandleR as a special
present! See if you can uncover any
A6suspicious placesR on the map!",
  "4.954.0" => "It's a secret to everybody!",
  "4.955.0" => "A6Goddess's HarpR: Use it on Goddess
Butterflies to make Gossip Stones appear.",
  "4.956.0" => "Search on the map.",
  "4.957.0" => "Now you have a A6CandleR, try searching
on the map. You can A6find new weaponsR
A6which can then be won as battle rewardsR. Move
to the map square indicated to start the search.",
  "4.958.0" => "Why there?",
  "4.959.0" => "Do you by any chance remember
The Legend of Zelda™ for the NES™?
Well...learning the secrets of that
game may prove very helpful here!",
  "4.960.0" => "Here, take one more A6CandleR as a special reward
this time and this time only! Try using it during
other searches to uncover A6suspicious placesR on
the map!",
  "4.961.0" => "Two-Player Co-op",
  "4.962.0" => "Each of the game modes can be played
cooperatively with two players.",
  "4.963.0" => "In co-op play, one player uses the TV screen
while the other player uses the GamePad.",
  "4.964.0" => "In order to enjoy two-player co-op, make sure
that both the Wii U GamePad and a second
controller are connected to the Wii U console.",
  "4.965.0" => "After connecting two controllers, the second
player can press PH on the Select Warrior
screen to join the game.",
  "4.966.0" => "You can change each player's controller
preferences in "Controller Settings" in the
Settings menu.",
  "4.967.0" => "Master Quest Rules",
  "4.968.0" => "Every battle on the A6Master Quest mapR
follows one of the special A6Master Quest rulesR.
Are you up to the challenge?",
  "4.969.0" => "A6Speed Run!R
Clear the battle within 20 minutes.",
  "4.970.0" => "A6No Healing!R
You cannot use potions, and no healing items
will appear.",
  "4.971.0" => "A6No Guarding!R
Guarding will not protect you from enemy hits.",
  "4.972.0" => "A6No Item Attacks!R
You cannot attack using bombs, the bow and
arrows, Hookshot, boomerang or hammer.",
  "4.973.0" => "A6Don't Get Hit!R
A single blow will put you at death's doorstep!
You'll need to make effective use of the special
A6ClockR item to freeze enemies. ",
  "4.974.0" => "The Clock",
  "4.975.0" => "Pick up the A6ClockR to freeze nearby enemies
for a while.",
  "4.976.0" => "Twilight Map Item Cards",
  "4.977.0" => "A6CompassR: Use this while searching to
identify where an Item Card can be used.",
  "4.978.0" => "A6LanternR: Use this on torches
to reveal hidden enemies.
A6BombR: Use this on boulders
to reveal hidden staircases.",
  "4.979.0" => "A6JarR: Use this on switches to reveal
hidden staircases.
A6Fishing RodR: Use this to catch fish
in bodies of water.",
  "4.980.0" => "A6ClawshotR: Use this to pull yourself
to a distant object.
A6SpinnerR: Use this on cog-shaped
holes to reveal hidden staircases.",
  "4.981.0" => "A6Water BombR: Use this on submerged
rocks to destroy them.
A6Digging MittsR: Use these on soft earth to
uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.982.0" => "A6OoccooR: Use this on a green portal
to warp to another location.
A6Tears of LightR: Use these to clear
away areas covered in Twilight.",
  "4.984.0" => "Twilight Rules",
  "4.985.0" => "Map squares covered in A6TwilightR will obscure
the positions of enemies on the battlefield map.
The Twilight is very dangerous!",
  "4.986.0" => "And remember, each battle has additional rules
in effect, so you'll have to be extra careful!",
  "4.987.0" => "A6No Special Attacks!R
Defeating enemies will not fill the Special Attack
gauge, and no Force Fragments will appear.",
  "4.988.0" => "A6No Focus Spirit!R
Magic Jars will not appear, so you will be
unable to fill your Magic gauge.",
  "4.989.0" => "A6No Item Attacks!R
You cannot attack using bombs, the bow and
arrows, Hookshot, boomerang or hammer.",
  "4.990.0" => "The Twilight Realm",
  "4.991.0" => "You'll encounter special A6Twilight rulesR in battles
taking place in areas covered in A6TwilightR.",
  "4.992.0" => "You can clear Twilight from a map square
by using a A6Tears of LightR Item Card on the
search screen.",
  "4.993.0" => "Warp Portals",
  "4.994.0" => "A handful of A6warp portalsR exist on the
Twilight Adventure map. Using them skillfully
will be the key to smooth adventuring.",
  "4.995.0" => "You will not be able to use red warp portals.
Win the battle to turn the portal green and
gain access to its warping powers.",
  "4.996.0" => "Use the A6OoccooR Item Card on green portals to
warp to other areas.",
  "4.997.0" => "Tears of Twilight",
  "4.998.0" => "This is a very unique Item Card. Use it to restore
Twilight to all areas it originally affected. It will only
appear once all the Twilight has been cleared from
the map, and can be activated on any map square.",
  "4.999.0" => "Twili Midna, Ruler of Twilight",
  "4.1000.0" => "During the Era of Twilight, Midna, the Twilight
Princess herself, joined the legendary hero in
saving both worlds of light and darkness.",
  "4.1001.0" => "With the battle won and the curse lifted, Midna
regained her true form, displaying her mysterious
beauty once more. As one of royal Twilight blood,
she has powers known only to the Twili people.",
  "4.1002.0" => "The ancient mirror she wields strengthens her
Twilight powers even further, meaning she no
longer has to rely on the Fused Shadow to
devastate her enemies on the battlefield.",
  "4.1003.0" => "Contests Against Other Forces",
  "4.1004.0" => "Rupee Fairies",
  "4.1005.0" => "The Termina Map",
  "4.1006.0" => "Owl Statues",
  "4.1007.0" => "Termina Map Item Cards",
  "4.1008.0" => "Giants",
  "4.1009.0" => "Majora's Power",
  "4.1010.0" => "In certain Adventure Mode battles, you'll A6competeR
against Other Forces to score more points or
complete objectives faster. The key to winning
is to be the best commander on the battlefield!",
  "4.1011.0" => "If you capture a Rupee Fairy, enemies will
start dropping a higher number of Rupees for
a limited amount of time.",
  "4.1012.0" => "Your A6timeR on the Termina Map will be A6limitedR.
The A6time counterR at the bottom of the map will
tick down by one hour for each battle you fight.",
  "4.1013.0" => "When the A6time counterR reaches A6zeroR,
the moon will fall and the entire map will A6resetR
to its starting state.",
  "4.1014.0" => "However, when the map resets, you will not lose
any experience, Rupees, weapons, materials, or
Item Cards you collected. You also keep your rank
on each completed map square.",
  "4.1015.0" => "The time counter and the moon's fall can only be
stopped by finding and defeating the A6Dark RulerR
who hides somewhere on the Termina Map.",
  "4.1016.0" => "Thus begins your quest to stop the moon
from falling and save Termina!",
  "4.1017.0" => "spare line",
  "4.1018.0" => "If you win a battle on a map square with an
A6owl statueR, the statue will activate and spread
out its wings.",
  "4.1019.0" => "If the moon falls and resets the map, any map
squares containing owl statues you've activated,
and any neighbouring, connected map squares,
will be unaffected.",
  "4.1020.0" => "A6CompassR: Use this while searching to
identify where an Item Card can be used.",
  "4.1021.0" => "A6Deku MaskR: Use this on flowers to
jump toward a neighboring map square.
A6Goron MaskR: Use this on switches
to reveal enemies.",
  "4.1022.0" => "A6Zora MaskR: Use this on whirlpools
to reveal enemies.",
  "4.1023.0" => "A6Mask of TruthR: Use this on the Search map
to double your defense for one battle.
A6Majora's MaskR: Use this on the Search map
to fill your Magic and SP gauges for one battle.",
  "4.1024.0" => "A6Deku StickR: Use this on torches to
reveal enemies.
A6BombR: Use this on boulders to uncover
hidden staircases.",
  "4.1025.0" => "A6Ice ArrowR: Use this on circles of flame
to uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.1026.0" => "A6Song of TimeR: Play this on the Search map
to reset all map squares to their starting state.
A6Inverted Song of TimeR: Play this on the Search map
to add 10 hours back to the clock.",
  "4.1027.0" => "A6GiantR: This is a very special Item Card!
There are only four hidden around Termina.",
  "4.1028.0" => "Use all four on the A6Clock TownR search screen
to reveal a hidden map square!",
  "4.1029.0" => "If you use the A6Mask of TruthR or A6Majora's MaskR
Item Cards on a map square, the square will
become affected by A6Majora's PowerR.",
  "4.1030.0" => "A6Temporary defense boost!R
The damage your warrior takes will be halved
for the extent of the battle.",
  "4.1031.0" => "A6SP and Magic gauges full!R
Your warrior's Special Attack and Magic gauges
will become full for the battle.",
  "4.1032.0" => "A6KO-count competitionR:
Compete to earn points by defeating enemies.
The lower number is your warrior's score, while
the one above it is your rival's score.",
  "4.1033.0" => "A6Rupee competitionR:
Compete to collect the most Rupees during battle.
Stronger enemies carry more Rupees!",
  "4.1034.0" => "A6Keep-taking competitionR:
Compete to capture the most keeps.
Cooperate with your allies to capture
as many as you possibly can!",
  "4.1035.0" => "Smithy",
  "4.1036.0" => "Skill Removal",
  "4.1037.0" => "Skill Appraisal",
  "4.1038.0" => "Selling Weapons",
  "4.1039.0" => "In the Smithy, you can customize your weapons
by fusing new skills onto them or by removing
existing skills.",
  "4.1040.0" => "A6Fuse WeaponsR:
Combine weapons to add skills.
A6Remove SkillsR:
Remove a skill from a weapon.",
  "4.1041.0" => "A6Appraise SkillsR:
Check the contents of a sealed skill.
A6Sell WeaponsR:
Sell a weapon for Rupees.",
  "4.1042.0" => "By removing a skill, you can change an unlocked
skill into an empty skill slot.",
  "4.1043.0" => "You can then fill that slot with other skills, so it's
a good way to create a weapon forged with the
skills best suited to your battle style.",
  "4.1044.0" => "However, removing a skill requires a lot of Rupees.
What's more, removed skills can never be restored,
so make sure to think twice before removing one.",
  "4.1045.0" => "By appraising a sealed weapon skill, you can
find out what the sealed skill actually is.",
  "4.1046.0" => "The Rupees required to appraise a sealed skill
change according to the KO count required to
unlock the skill.",
  "4.1047.0" => "When you sell a weapon, you will receive 
an amount of Rupees dependent on the skills
attached to that weapon.",
  "4.1048.0" => "The weapons you sell will be lost. Also, sealed
skills and empty skill slots do not contribute to
the weapon's value, so keep that in mind!",
  "4.1049.0" => "Young Link, a Determined Youth",
  "4.1050.0" => "The land of Termina faced imminent destruction
from a maniacal masked figure and a furious moon,
but a young hero named Link appeared just in time
to summon the four giants and set things right.",
  "4.1051.0" => "Link originally found himself in Termina while
in search of someone dear to him. The Skull
Kid stole the Ocarina of Time from him and
set the events of Majora's Mask in motion.",
  "4.1052.0" => "Despite his youth, Link is a formidable warrior,
possessing mastery of a sword. He also comes
equipped with the Fierce Deity Mask, an object
that allows him to turn into a powerful spirit.",
  "4.1053.0" => "Tingle, the Reincarnated Fairy?",
  "4.1054.0" => "Who is this man? Is it really a man? He says that
he's actually a fairy, but he doesn't necessarily
look much like a fairy... Are there 35-year-old
fairies? Is Tingle one of them?",
  "4.1055.0" => "Despite Tingle's...unorthodox fashion choices,
he has a pure and innocent heart. He genuinely
seeks to help his father by selling maps he made
while floating around Termina by balloon.",
  "4.1056.0" => "With his balloon and endless supplies of tricks,
Tingle is a surprisingly competent addition to
any group of warriors. If you're lucky, you may
even hear a "Kooloo-Limpah" in battle!",
  "4.1057.0" => "Battle Score",
  "4.1058.0" => "Challenge Mode Rewards",
  "4.1059.0" => "Ganon Controls",
  "4.1060.0" => "Cucco Controls",
  "4.1061.0" => "Survival Battle",
  "4.1062.0" => "Boss Attack Items",
  "4.1063.0" => "Fireball",
  "4.1064.0" => "Ganon Bomb",
  "4.1065.0" => "Fury Horn",
  "4.1066.0" => "Burning Breath",
  "4.1067.0" => "Dark Giant Bosses",
  "4.1068.0" => "In A6Challenge ModeR, battle results will be
separately recorded for each battle and each
warrior as a A6Battle ScoreR.",
  "4.1069.0" => "The Battle Score will only be updated
whenever you beat your previous best
A6Rupee TotalR!",
  "4.1070.0" => "Aim for the highest scores possible!
How's that for a challenge?",
  "4.1071.0" => "Challenge Mode",
  "4.1072.0" => "In A6Boss ChallengeR and A6Ganon's FuryR, you can
obtain special rewards by attaining A6A RankR in
battles marked with a reward icon.",
  "4.1073.0" => "Challenge Mode Rewards",
  "4.1074.0" => "Challenge Mode Rewards",
  "4.1075.0" => "Challenge Mode Rewards",
  "4.1076.0" => "When playing as A6GanonR, certain controls are
different when compared to playing as a regular
warrior.",
  "4.1077.0" => "Pb A6Regular AttackR: Swing your paws to strike.
Keep pressing to attack up to three times in a row.
Pc A6Strong AttackR: A forward-facing electric attack,
usable twice in a row. Can follow a Regular Attack.",
  "4.1078.0" => "Pg A6Spin AttackR: Spin with arms extended to knock
back all surrounding enemies.
P9 A6Charge AttackR: Gather power, then charge
forward. Can follow a Regular Attack.",
  "4.1079.0" => "P5 A6Select Boss AttackR:
Selects the Boss Attack that you'll use.
Pi A6Use Boss AttackR:
Uses the currently selected Boss Attack.",
  "4.1080.0" => "When playing as a A6CuccoR, certain controls are
different when compared to playing as a regular
warrior.",
  "4.1081.0" => "Pb A6Regular AttackR: Peck at enemies with your beak!
Keep pressing the button for a two-peck combo.
Pc A6Strong AttackR: A more powerful peck. Hits foes
in front of you, sending them flying.",
  "4.1082.0" => "Pg, Pi, P5, P9:
Cuccos don't need these buttons, so ignore them!",
  "4.1083.0" => "You can also see these controls in the
A6Check CombosR menu.",
  "4.1084.0" => "In A6Survival BattlesR, you won't be able to use
potions, and won't have any chances to regain
health, even if you level up mid-battle.",
  "4.1085.0" => "In addition, healing items won't appear, with
the exception of ones brought by A6Heart
Transport TroopsR.",
  "4.1086.0" => "Survival Battle",
  "4.1087.0" => "Survival Battle",
  "4.1088.0" => "By picking up the A6Boss Attack itemsR dropped
by defeated Giant Bosses, you gain the ability to
use A6Boss AttacksR until the battle ends.",
  "4.1089.0" => "Hitting each Giant Boss with the Boss Attack
it's A6weak toR lets you force the boss into a
A6downed stateR.",
  "4.1090.0" => "Dropped Items in Ganon's Fury",
  "4.1091.0" => "Dropped Items in Ganon's Fury",
  "4.1092.0" => "Shoot a A6FireballR from your right hand.
This can put A6ArgorokR into a downed state.",
  "4.1093.0" => "Dodongo Item",
  "4.1094.0" => "Dodongo Item",
  "4.1095.0" => "Dodongo Item",
  "4.1096.0" => "Launch a A6Ganon BombR from your left hand.
This can put A6King DodongoR into a downed state.",
  "4.1097.0" => "Gohma Item",
  "4.1098.0" => "Gohma Item",
  "4.1099.0" => "Gohma Item",
  "4.1100.0" => "Fire the A6Fury HornR on your shoulders.
This can put A6GohmaR into a downed state.",
  "4.1101.0" => "Manhandla Item",
  "4.1102.0" => "Manhandla Item",
  "4.1103.0" => "Manhandla Item",
  "4.1104.0" => "Spew A6Burning BreathR from your mouth.
This can put A6ManhandlaR into a downed state.",
  "4.1105.0" => "Argorok Item",
  "4.1106.0" => "Argorok Item",
  "4.1107.0" => "Argorok Item",
  "4.1108.0" => "A6Dark Giant BossesR, such as Dark King Dodongo
or Dark Gohma, cannot be put in a A6downed stateR
with items or techniques.",
  "4.1109.0" => "To defeat these A6fearsome foesR, you must evade 
their attacks and A6attack without using itemsR
whenever the opportunity presents itself!",
  "4.1112.0" => "Additions to Challenge Mode",
  "4.1113.0" => "By clearing battles in A6Boss ChallengeR and
A6Ganon's FuryR, you can unlock additional
A6battle typesR in Challenge Mode.",
  "4.1114.0" => "Attaining A6A RankR in battles gives you 
harder fights to challenge yourself with.",
  "4.1115.0" => "You can also see these controls in the
A6Check CombosR menu.",
  "4.1116.0" => "Ganon's Fury can only be played A6single-playerR.
It cannot be played co-operatively.",
  "4.1117.0" => "Cucco's Fury can only be played A6single-playerR.
It cannot be played co-operatively.",
  "4.1118.0" => "Changing Warriors",
  "4.1119.0" => "Tap a A6warrior's faceR on the touch 
screen to change which warrior you're
directly controlling.",
  "4.1120.0" => "You can only select a warrior when their face is
lit up. A dark face means you cannot control
that warrior!",
  "4.1121.0" => "There may be times when the number of warriors
you can control increases as scenarios progress.",
  "4.1122.0" => "Ocarina",
  "4.1123.0" => "Use the Ocarina to warp to active A6Owl StatuesR.",
  "4.1124.0" => "To activate an Owl Statue, approach the statue
and press the button displayed on screen.",
  "4.1125.0" => "Smash Boost Power",
  "4.1126.0" => "If A6multiple playable warriors gather near a GiantR
A6BossR, they'll receive all kinds of effects. The more
warriors gathered, the strong the effect becomes!",
  "4.1127.0" => "If A6two playable warriorsR get together, 50%
of their A6Magic Meters will instantly fillR! Plus,
A6you will be able to refill the Magic MeterR
A6just by attacking enemiesR!",
  "4.1128.0" => "When A6three playable warriorsR gather,
nearby A6Giant Bosses' weak point gauges will
deplete fasterR.",
  "4.1129.0" => "When A6four playable warriorsR gather,
the A6Giant Bosses will receive greater
amounts of damageR.",
  "4.1130.0" => "Hammer Switches",
  "4.1131.0" => "With a A6hammerR you can press a switch to trigger
various events. You can also attack certain foes.",
  "4.1132.0" => "Stone Heads",
  "4.1133.0" => "These large stone heads can't be broken by regular
attacks or items. You'll have to use special
devices to destroy them.",
  "4.1134.0" => "Missions",
  "4.1135.0" => "There are times when A6multiple missionsR will trigger
at the same time. You can see what they are by
tapping the Mission Bar on the Touch Screen.",
  "4.1136.0" => "Side missions are only occasionally triggered.
Failing a side mission won't have major effects
on the battle, so feel free to try them out
if you're feeling particularly adventurous!",
  "4.1137.0" => "Commanding Multiple Warriors",
  "4.1138.0" => "You can A6commandR playable warriors to march to
given destinations, even when you aren't directly
controlling them.",
  "4.1139.0" => "Touch the map on the Touch Screen to set
the A6target destinationR for a warrior.",
  "4.1140.0" => "After selecting a warrior, tap the location you'd
like to set as the destination, then confirm using
the touch screen or with P0 to start the
warrior moving.",
  "4.1141.0" => "Playable Warriors",
  "4.1142.0" => "If any of your playable warriors flee,
you will lose the battle.",
  "4.1143.0" => "You can check which warriors are playable by
looking at the face icons on the Touch Screen.",
  "4.1144.0" => "Even if it is not written explicitly in a scenario's
loss conditions, remember that a playable warrior
fleeing will always cause a loss!",
  "4.1145.0" => "Advanced Summoners",
  "4.1146.0" => "An A6advanced summonerR is a dangerous enemy
that can call powerful units one after another.
Defeating them quickly is key!",
  "4.1147.0" => "Assault Troopers",
  "4.1148.0" => "A6Assault TroopersR are enemies that retreat after
assaulting a target and inflicting damage. Defeat
them before they arrive at their destination!",
  "4.1149.0" => "Rally Troops",
  "4.1150.0" => "A6Rally TroopsR raise the morale of the enemy.
Think of them like cheerleading squads!",
  "4.1151.0" => "Some raise the enemy's morale slowly over
time, while others raise their forces' morale
right after they appear.",
  "4.1152.0" => "Enemies with high morale are incredibly powerful,
so defeat Rally Troops quickly!",
  "4.1153.0" => "Messengers",
  "4.1154.0" => "When A6MessengersR arrive at their destination, they
call reinforcements and then leave the battlefield.",
  "4.1155.0" => "Keep Saboteurs",
  "4.1156.0" => "A6Keep SaboteursR are enemy units that can
quickly capture keeps.",
  "4.1157.0" => "If you see these troops marching towards a
keep, you need to act fast and defeat them
right away!",
  "4.1158.0" => "The Great Sea Map",
  "4.1159.0" => "On the Great Sea map, there are places where a
A6headwindR is blocking the way, stopping you from 
moving forward. Certain battles also include
special rules you have to follow.",
  "4.1160.0" => "On a map square with a headwind blowing,
using the A6Wind WakerR item card on the search
screen will remove the headwind and allow you
to go full steam ahead!",
  "4.1161.0" => "A6Single-hit KOs!R
On squares with Big Octos, a single hit will put
your warriors at death's door! Avoid attacks and
watch for enemy movements!",
  "4.1162.0" => "A6Double damage!R
On map squares with warships, warriors will
receive twice as much damage as normal!",
  "4.1163.0" => "A6No item attacks!R
On map squares with tornadoes, warriors won't
be able to use bombs, the bow and arrow, the
Hookshot, the boomerang, or the hammer!",
  "4.1164.0" => "Great Sea Item Cards",
  "4.1165.0" => "A6CompassR: Use this while searching to
identify where an Item Card can be used.",
  "4.1166.0" => "A6Wind WakerR: Use this on the search map
to stop headwinds.",
  "4.1167.0" => "A6CannonR: Use this to sink warships.
A6BoomerangR: Use this to defeat Big Octos.",
  "4.1168.0" => "A6Hero's BowR: Use this to dispel tornadoes.
A6Salvage ArmR: Use this on rings of light to
reveal hidden treasure.",
  "4.1169.0" => "A6Hyoi PearR: Use this on seagulls to
reveal secret treasure.
A6Deku LeafR: Use this on windmills to
uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.1170.0" => "A6Sea MapR: Use this where you see
sea spray in order to reveal enemies.
A6Power BraceletR: Use this on stone heads
to reveal enemies.",
  "4.1171.0" => "My Fairy Mode",
  "4.1172.0" => "A6Companion FairiesR are partners who use
powerful magic and skills to help you on your
adventure.",
  "4.1173.0" => "You will meet all kinds of fairies during
Adventure Mode battles. These fairies are hidden in
various jars in enemy keeps during these battles.",
  "4.1174.0" => "Bringing a companion fairy into battle allows you
to use A6Fairy MagicR. The effects of the magic
will become more powerful as the fairy's level
increases.",
  "4.1175.0" => "The fairies each have an elemental attribute:
Fire, Water, Lightning, Light, or Darkness. When
a fairy matches the recommended element of a
stage, her Fairy Magic will be even stronger!",
  "4.1176.0" => "By nurturing your companion fairies, you will
be able to use various A6Rental SkillsR that
produce different helpful effects in battle.",
  "4.1177.0" => "Collect and nurture fairies with all kinds of
personality traits to really give yourself an
edge in battle!",
  "4.1178.0" => "Nurturing Fairy Companions",
  "4.1179.0" => "In My Fairy mode, you can nurture and clothe your
A6companion fairiesR and switch or exchange
their various Rental Skills.",
  "4.1180.0" => "A6Dining RoomR: You can increase your fairies'
stats by giving them A6foodR.",
  "4.1181.0" => "A6SalonR: You can equip your fairies
with A6fairy clothingR.",
  "4.1182.0" => "A6SchoolR: You can change your fairies'
A6Rental SkillsR.",
  "4.1183.0" => "A6PartyR: You can use local communication to
A6trade Rental SkillsR with other players.",
  "4.1184.0" => "Food",
  "4.1185.0" => "Feed A6foodR to your fairies to
improve their stats.",
  "4.1186.0" => "You can get A6foodR by defeating enemies
or, in Adventure Battles, by acquiring it from jars
in enemy keeps.",
  "4.1187.0" => "Dining Room",
  "4.1188.0" => "In the Dining Room, you can feed your fairies.",
  "4.1189.0" => "Select the food on the Touch Screen and use
P0, or drag the food over to the fairy
to feed them.",
  "4.1190.0" => "Refreshing My Fairies",
  "4.1191.0" => "Once a fairy has reached A6level 99R,
use P3 to A6RefreshR her, which allows
you to retrain her from Level 1.",
  "4.1192.0" => "By refreshing, you can carry over 10% of their
stats, as well as any Rental Skills they've learned.",
  "4.1193.0" => "Fairy Clothing",
  "4.1194.0" => "Use A6fairy clothingR to change how a fairy looks.
There are five types of clothes: tops, bottoms,
decorations, headgear, and accessories.",
  "4.1195.0" => "Each fairy clothing item has one effect that will
change either the amount of damage inflicted by
Fairy Magic, or the amount of Magic Power used.",
  "4.1196.0" => "Salon",
  "4.1197.0" => "In the A6SalonR, you can dress your fairies in all
kinds of fairy clothing to give them a fashion
style fit for a fairy.",
  "4.1198.0" => "Select fairy clothing with P4 and change an
item with P0. Register items in your favorites
by pressing P3.",
  "4.1199.0" => "School",
  "4.1200.0" => "In the A6SchoolR, you can change your
companion fairies' Rental Skills.",
  "4.1201.0" => "Fairies can learn different Rental Skills depending
on which five of the different fairy personality traits
they have. You can check the personality traits
and their current values on the radar chart.",
  "4.1202.0" => "Any personality traits that the companion fairy
doesn't have will be displayed in red. You can
change one of the fairy's personality traits
each time you refresh her.",
  "4.1203.0" => "If your My Fairy doesn't have the personality trait
required for a Rental Skill, she won't be able to
learn that skill.",
  "4.1204.0" => "Rental Skills",
  "4.1205.0" => "Rental Skills are powerful abilities that
companion fairies can learn. Each fairy can learn
up to four Rental Skills by borrowing them from
other players.",
  "4.1206.0" => "You can use A6Rental SkillsR in battle by
selecting them as you would an item, and 
pressing Pi.",
  "4.1207.0" => "Different Rental Skills have different effects,
like temporarily stopping the Special Attack
gauge from decreasing or allowing you to be
revived just once after being KO'd.",
  "4.1208.0" => "The strength of Rental Skills will increase as
your companion fairy levels up.",
  "4.1209.0" => "Party",
  "4.1210.0" => "In Parties, you can use local communication
to borrow Rental Skills from other players.",
  "4.1211.0" => "A6Invite people nearbyR:
Search for other players with whom you can trade
Rental Skills. When you've found a partner, start
the trade with P0.",
  "4.1212.0" => "A6Search for invitationsR:
Find players searching for partners to
exchange Rental Skills with. Select the
user's name and make the request with P0.",
  "4.1213.0" => "Once you find a partner, choose the fairy
you want to send over and make the exchange.",
  "4.1214.0" => "Fairy Magic",
  "4.1215.0" => "Tap the icon on the bottom left of the touch
screen to use up your Magic gauge and trigger
powerful A6Fairy MagicR!",
  "4.1216.0" => "Using Fairy Magic will release an explosive
attack that corresponds to the companion fairy's
elemental type.",
  "4.1217.0" => "As a companion fairy grows, she can learn to
cause additional effects when using Fairy Magic.
A6BombosR:
Lower defense for enemy troops within range.",
  "4.1218.0" => "A6EtherR:
Raise defense for allied troops within range.
A6QuakeR:
Lower speed for enemy troops within range.",
  "4.1219.0" => "A6ShineR:
Restore health for allied troops within range.
A6ShadeR:
Deal damage to enemy troops within range.",
  "4.1220.0" => "As companion fairies level up, they will learn the
additional effect corresponding to the gained
attributes. Doubling up on the same effect
will give the effect twice the power!",
  "4.1221.0" => "Extra-Effective Item Attacks",
  "4.1222.0" => "Some enemies leave an opening before performing
certain attacks. When the enemy is open, an icon
will appear above them hinting at the right item
to use at that time.",
  "4.1223.0" => "Use the correct item attack during one of these
openings, and the enemy's Weak Point gauge will
be revealed while the surprised enemy rampages,
damaging other nearby foes.",
  "4.1224.0" => "This is a highly effective technique that gives
you a chance at performing a Weak Point Smash,
while also damaging surrounding enemies.
Make the most of every opportunity!",
  "4.1225.0" => "Toon Link, the Hero of Winds",
  "4.1226.0" => "With portals opened to other dimensions, another
Link slipped through--the legendary Hero of Winds
from the Era of the Great Sea.",
  "4.1227.0" => "While trying to save his kidnapped sister, he
challenged the ruler of evil. Helped by a red boat
and a pirate crew, and controlling the wind, he
traveled far and wide across the Great Sea.",
  "4.1228.0" => "Quick on his feet and light in the air, Toon
Link excels at speedy combos with his
short sword and his trusty Deku Leaf.
He may be small, but he packs a punch!",
  "4.1229.0" => "Tetra, the Pirate Leader",
  "4.1230.0" => "With a portal to the Era of the Great Sea opened,
the captain of the terrors of the sea rushed
through and joined the legendary hero in his cause.",
  "4.1231.0" => "Despite her relatively young age, Tetra is
already an accomplished and fearsome
pirate captain, regularly leading a crew of
six into and out of certain danger.",
  "4.1232.0" => "She carries a cutlass in one hand and a
magic-infused pistol in the other, making
her deadly both up close and from afar.
No one disrespects a pirate!",
  "4.1233.0" => "King Daphnes, the King of Red Lions",
  "4.1234.0" => "With a portal to the Era of the Great Sea opened,
the King of Red Lions himself came through to aid
the legendary hero in his cause.",
  "4.1235.0" => "King Daphnes Nohansen Hyrule was an ancient
land's final king, forced to watch his home
fade into legend under the Great Sea. He also
helped Toon Link in the guise of a red boat.",
  "4.1236.0" => "Harking back to his time as that red boat,
King Daphnes purges evil from this world
with a powerful sail, and even changes
back into a boat during certain attacks.",
  "4.1237.0" => "Skull Kid, Majora's Puppet",
  "4.1238.0" => "In three days' time, the moon will fall and
destroy the land of Termina. At least, it
will if Skull Kid has any say in the matter.
Thankfully, Young Link put an end to that.",
  "4.1239.0" => "Skull Kid is a mischievous little imp who inherited
fearsome powers after stealing the cursed Majora's
Mask. Despite causing widespread destruction and
chaos, he is actually very protective of his friends.",
  "4.1240.0" => "Equipped with an ocarina, a trumpet, his two fairy
companions, Tatl and Tael, and of course the
terrifying power of Majora's Mask itself, Skull
Kid is a serious threat to anyone around him.",
  "4.1241.0" => "StreetPass Links",
  "4.1242.0" => "Other players using StreetPass features may
appear on your map as alternate-colored Links.
 Winning your battle will help them out!",
  "4.1243.0" => "Battles waged on a map with StreetPass
Links are much more difficult, but you're
also awarded more powerful weapons and
other beneficial items.",
  "4.1244.0" => "On maps with StreetPass Links from your
friends, you will acquire better rewards still.",
  "4.1245.0" => "Statues and Korok Trees",
  "4.1246.0" => "Some paths are blocked by Statues or Korok
Trees. Look for nearby switches to open up
the paths.",
  "4.1247.0" => "Once a path is open, both allies and enemies
can pass through.",
  "4.1248.0" => "Great Sea Rules",
  "4.1249.0" => "The Great Sea is littered with all kinds of A6hazardsR .
These will cause different rules to apply during
battles waged on map squares containing them,
so keep your wits about you!",
  "4.1250.0" => "Luckily, you can also use the A6cannonR, A6boomerangR
or A6Hero's BowR item cards to get rid of
these hazards.",
  "4.1251.0" => "A6Don't get hit!R
On squares with Big Octos, a single hit will put
your warrior's life in danger! Avoid attacks and
watch for enemy movements!",
  "4.1252.0" => "A6Double damage!R
On map squares with warships, warriors will
receive twice as much damage as normal!",
  "4.1253.0" => "A6No item attacks!R
On map squares with tornadoes, warriors won't
be able to use bombs, the bow and arrows, the
Hookshot, the boomerang, or the hammer!",
  "4.1254.0" => "Select multiple characters to give
marching orders to a whole group.",
  "4.1255.0" => "You can also select A6CommandR on the
information screen to issue commands.",
  "4.1256.0" => "If you find a Messenger advancing toward a
keep, you should defeat it right away!",
  "4.1257.0" => "Defeat Giant Bosses by gathering the
strength of multiple allied warriors!",
  "4.1258.0" => "In A6Adventure Mode battlesR, certain enemy
keeps have fairy clothing hidden inside. Capture
lots of enemy keeps to reveal hidden chests
and get at their treasure!",
  "4.1259.0" => "Every time you refresh, the fairy's magic
gets a 1% damage boost! Nurture your
favorite companion fairy and give yourself an
advantage in battle!",
  "4.1260.0" => "You can also A6change one of the fairy's
personality traitsR when you refresh her. The
Rental Skills a companion fairy can acquire
change according to her trait combination.",
  "4.1261.0" => "You can check what trait combinations
are required for particular Rental Skills at the
companion fairy A6SchoolR.",
  "4.1262.0" => "Aim for the Rental Skills that best suit your
playstyle, and raise fairy companions that are
all your own!",
  "4.1263.0" => "Your companion fairies also have a A6TrustR level
which you can increase by giving them food.
There are even some Rental Skills that become
more powerful as a fairy's Trust in you grows.",
  "4.1264.0" => "Chuchus",
  "4.1265.0" => "Chuchus can't be defeated with conventional
attacks, and will damage you if you try.
Try to find a different way to defeat them!",
  "4.1266.0" => "Dashing",
  "4.1267.0" => "If you tilt PJ and keep moving, after a short
while your warrior will break into a dash.
This lets you move much faster.",
  "4.1268.0" => "You can also start dashing by evading with Pd,
then continuing to move while holding Pd.",
  "4.1269.0" => "Health",
  "4.1270.0" => "Zoomed Mini Map (Upper Screen)",
  "4.1271.0" => "Mini Map (Touch Screen)",
  "4.1272.0" => "Destination Icon",
  "4.1273.0" => "Enemy Icon",
  "4.1274.0" => "Giant Boss Icon",
  "4.1275.0" => "The hearts lined up on the upper screen represent
health for the warrior you are controlling.
The battle will be lost if a controllable warrior's
hearts are depleted, so be careful!",
  "4.1276.0" => "The mini map on the upper screen will show you
what's happening near the warrior you are
controlling.",
  "4.1277.0" => "Check the enemy you need to defeat by looking
at the animation.",
  "4.1278.0" => "Even if you are not near the enemies
you need to defeat, you can see in which
direction they are located.",
  "4.1279.0" => "On the Touch Screen mini map you can check the
overall battle situation. Check the locations of
A1allied (blue)R and A2enemy (red)R troops in order
to defeat enemies efficiently!",
  "4.1280.0" => "Playable warriors are indicated by arrows.
The A1allied commanderR is represented by a
A1blue flagR. If that commander flees, you will lose
the battle, so pay attention!",
  "4.1281.0" => "The square icons appearing on the mini map are
keeps. Your army is at an advantage when there
are more blue keeps. Capture the A2red enemy
keepsR and increase the number of A1blue keepsR!",
  "4.1282.0" => "There are some occasions when the keep gates
are closed. Some gates never seem to open, but
capture keeps or defeat certain enemies and open
they will.",
  "4.1283.0" => "Diamonds mark outposts. Enemies will continuously
appear at outposts, so swing the tide of battle to
your advantage by taking A2enemy outposts (red)R and
making them into A1allied outposts (blue)R.",
  "4.1284.0" => "Places where an × is flashing mark the
A6destinationR of the current mission. Move a
controllable warrior to that location to complete
the mission!",
  "4.1285.0" => "Enemies located where there is a flashing circle
must be A6defeatedR for the current mission.
Move a controllable warrior to that location
to quickly defeat the target!",
  "4.1286.0" => "A flashing square marks a location that must
be A6capturedR for the current mission.
Move a controllable warrior to that location
to quickly take that keep!",
  "4.1287.0" => "Enemy icons with black edges are
A2strong enemiesR that could cause trouble for
your allies. If you see one, make sure to
defeat it posthaste!",
  "4.1288.0" => "Double black edges indicate an enemy of A2truly
outstanding powerR! These foes can be the
difference between victory and defeat. Only
challenge them after taking stock of the situation!",
  "4.1289.0" => "Skull icons indicate Giant Boss enemies. Even a 
single one can A2dominate the battlefieldR. They
have lots of health and power, so defeating them
should be your priority. Watch their attack patterns!",
  "4.1290.0" => "Keeps with castle icons are the armies' main
bases. If your allied base falls to enemy attack,
you will lose the battle. Keep an eye on your
base, and come running if it needs you!",
  "4.1291.0" => "The A2red flag iconR shows the A2enemy commanderR.
Defeat them and lead your forces to victory!",
  "4.1292.0" => "If P5 is set to Camera Control using the
Customize Controls option in Control Settings,
press P5 while A6targetingR an enemy
to change the target of the camera.",
  "4.1293.0" => "A6TargetingR is useful when striking an
enemy's opening or evading a giant enemy's attack.
Use it skillfully to gain an advantage.",
  "4.1294.0" => "Your A6battle rankR will be determined by your
Battle Record when you gain victory in a battle.
There are three levels of A6battle ranksR:
A6A, B, CR in order from best to worst.",
  "4.1295.0" => "If you win a battle with A6battle rank BR,
your character will be able to move in directions
where there is a A6B arrow or C arrow.R",
  "4.1296.0" => "Depending on your battle rank after finishing a 
battle, more direction options may open for you.
Strengthen your character, and expand your map!",
  "4.1297.0" => "Basic Controls",
  "4.1298.0" => "Pb: Attack enemies
Pc: Use more powerful attacks
Pd: Evade enemy attacks
Pe: Use Special Attacks to overwhelm foes",
  "4.1299.0" => "You can change the button settings by entering
"Settings" from the main menu and selecting
"Button Settings" in "Controller Settings".",
  "4.1300.0" => "P5 can be used either to cycle through items
or to control the camera. Switch between the two
by entering "Settings" from the main menu and
selecting "Button Settings" in "Controller Settings".",
  "4.1301.0" => "If you find fairies in jars, they will become your
companions. Gather lots of fairies, and work with 
them to overcome challenges on your adventures!",
  "4.1302.0" => "Your companion fairies will become stronger as you
feed them lots of food and outfit them with fairy
clothing.",
  "4.1303.0" => "Give yourself an advantage in battle by
collecting food and clothing to strengthen
your companion fairies!",
  "4.1304.0" => "As you progress through Adventure Mode,
you can find more and better kinds of Food.
Collect as many as you can to nurture your fairy
into the ideal companion!",
  "4.1305.0" => "A6HammerR: Use this on switches to
reveal hidden enemies.
A6HookshotR: Use this on distant targets to
pull yourself to them.",
  "4.1306.0" => "To see which battles give you a chance of getting
A6FoodR, press P3 on the main Adventure Mode
map to switch between the various spoils icons
until you find the right ones.",
  "4.1307.0" => "Break certain jars on the battlefield to reveal the
Food hidden within! Furthermore, Food that you've
found in a jar at least once before will have a
chance of appearing when you defeat enemies!",
  "4.1308.0" => "Medli, Sage of Earth",
  "4.1309.0" => "A world of tiny islands strewn across a vast sea...
A girl belonging to the race of Rito used her wings
and treasured harp to help the hero who traveled
the Great Sea in the world of the Wind Waker.",
  "4.1310.0" => "Hailing from Dragon Roost Island, Medli may
be a tender-hearted and courteous attendant
to the sky spirit, but she finds great courage
in the face of danger.",
  "4.1311.0" => "When she plays her harp she can manipulate the
very wind itself to attack enemies in a wide area.
Aside from this she can sprout her wings from
her arms to attack enemies both high and low!",
  "4.1312.0" => "Master Wind Waker Map",
  "4.1313.0" => "Your progress through the Master Wind
Waker Map will sometimes be blocked
by a strong A6headwindR.",
  "4.1314.0" => "On a map square with a headwind blowing,
using the A6Wind WakerR item card on the search
screen will remove the headwind and allow you
to go full steam ahead!",
  "4.1315.0" => "Certain battles on the Master Wind Waker Map
include additional A6Great Sea rulesR or
A6Endless Night rulesR. Challenge yourself
to them for a real swashbuckling adventure!",
  "4.1316.0" => "On maps where Great Sea rules apply, 
you can use the appropriate item card to get rid of
the A6sea hazardR and lift the restrictions.",
  "4.1317.0" => "Endless Night Rules",
  "4.1318.0" => "Many of the battles you will wage on the
A6Master Wind Waker MapR will
include special A6Endless Night rulesR.
Be brave and give them a shot!",
  "4.1319.0" => "A6Speed Run!R
Complete the battle within 20 minutes.",
  "4.1320.0" => "A6No Healing!R
You cannot use potions, and no healing items
will appear.",
  "4.1321.0" => "A6No Guarding!R
Guarding will not protect you from enemy hits.",
  "4.1322.0" => "A6No Fairy Magic!R
You cannot use Fairy Magic.
",
  "4.1323.0" => "A6No Special Attacks!R
Defeating enemies will not fill the Special Attack
gauge, and no Force Fragments will appear.",
  "4.1324.0" => "A6No Focus Spirit!R
Magic Jars will not appear, so you will be
unable to fill your Magic gauge.",
  "4.1325.0" => "A6No Rental Skills!R
You will not be able to use Rental Skills.",
  "4.1326.0" => "Master Wind Waker Map Item Cards",
  "4.1327.0" => "Marin, Songstress of Koholint Island",
  "4.1328.0" => "After rescuing a youth washed up on the shores of
Koholint Island, Marin, a young woman from
Mabe Village, helped wake the Wind Fish from its
nightmare in the world of Link's Awakening.",
  "4.1329.0" => "Everyone on Koholint Island adores Marin, but she
wants nothing more than to travel across the sea
and visit distant lands. She loves to sing, her voice
bringing cheer to humans and animals alike.",
  "4.1330.0" => "In battle she wields her bell, which is mightier
than it first appears. She attacks enemies with
the shock waves it emits, and can even summon
the power of the Wind Fish to aid her.",
  "4.1331.0" => "Koholint Island Map",
  "4.1332.0" => "The Wind Fish slumbers in its egg on the Koholint
Island Map, trapped in the throes of a A6NightmareR.
The Nightmare will stand in your way as you seek
those responsible. Dispel it to wake the Wind Fish!",
  "4.1333.0" => "When the Nightmare looms, use the A6Instruments
of the SirensR items from the Search screen to
dispel it, clearing the way for you to move forward.",
  "4.1334.0" => "The A6egg counterR at the bottom of the
screen will increase by one every time you use
an instrument of the Sirens.",
  "4.1335.0" => "By using all eight instruments you'll be able to
wake the Wind Fish, freeing it from its Nightmares
and driving them away for good.",
  "4.1336.0" => "Track down all eight instruments and awaken the
Wind Fish from its slumber, then seek out the
ruler of the Nightmares lurking somewhere on the
map and defeat him once and for all!",
  "4.1337.0" => "Instruments of the Sirens",
  "4.1338.0" => "Use the A6Instruments of the SirensR on map
squares where the Nightmare looms to dispel it,
allowing you to move forward.",
  "4.1339.0" => "Using an A6Instrument of the SirensR will
also cause a A6Siren PowerR to take effect
across the entire map. A Siren Power provides
advantages to all battles fought while it's active.",
  "4.1340.0" => "There are eight instruments in total, and each
one has a unique Siren Power. Use the instruments
wisely to give yourself an advantage in battle!",
  "4.1341.0" => "A Siren Power will last for a A6limited amount of
timeR. The number on the instrument counter
below the map will decrease by one each battle,
and the Siren Power will wear off when it hits 0.",
  "4.1342.0" => "One Siren Power cannot overwrite another and
only one can be active at a time. Once you
activate a Siren Power you need to wait for it to
wear off naturally, so be sure to plan ahead!",
  "4.1343.0" => "However, the Instruments of the Sirens' true
power still seems to be locked away...
Could it be linked in some way to awakening
the Wind Fish?",
  "4.1344.0" => "Nightmares",
  "4.1345.0" => "The A6NightmareR will shroud the enemies
on certain squares, preventing you from fighting
there until it's dispelled.",
  "4.1346.0" => "To eliminate a Nightmare, use one of the
A6Instruments of the SirensR item cards
from the Search screen on that square.",
  "4.1347.0" => "As long as the Wind Fish slumbers, Nightmares
will continue reappearing one by one. Collect all
eight instruments and awaken the Wind Fish to
vanquish the Nightmare once and for all!",
  "4.1348.0" => "Koholint Island Map Item Cards",
  "4.1349.0" => "A6CompassR: Use this while searching to
identify where an Item Card can be used.",
  "4.1350.0" => "A6Grandpa UlriraR: Use this on a Phone Booth
to uncover hidden treasures.
A6Power BraceletR: Use this on heavy rocks or
tombstones to uncover hidden stairways.",
  "4.1351.0" => "A6Magic PowderR: Use this on a torch to
open the way toward an adjacent map square.",
  "4.1352.0" => "A6Full Moon CelloR: Use this on the Search
screen to fill the Special Attack gauge.
A6Conch HornR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily reduce damage taken.",
  "4.1353.0" => "A6Sea Lily BellR: Use this on the Search
screen to fill the Magic gauge.
A6Surf HarpR: Use this on the Search screen
to temporarily increase experience earned.",
  "4.1354.0" => "A6Wind MarimbaR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily increase Rupees gained.
A6Coral TriangleR: Use this on the Search screen
to temporarily increase the amount of Food found.",
  "4.1355.0" => "A6Organ of Evening CalmR: Use on the Search
screen to temporarily increase the Material drop rate.
A6Thunder DrumR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily increase the weapon drop rate.",
  "4.1356.0" => "Siren Powers",
  "4.1357.0" => "Using an A6Instruments of the SirensR item
card from the Search screen will activate a
A6Siren PowerR across the entire map. This
power will provide an advantage during battle.",
  "4.1358.0" => "Only one Siren Power can be active at a time
and one Siren Power cannot overwrite another.",
  "4.1359.0" => "A6Full Moon CelloR: Use this on the Search
screen to fill the Special Attack gauge.
A6Conch HornR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily reduce damage taken.",
  "4.1360.0" => "A6Sea Lily BellR: Use this on the Search
screen to fill the Magic gauge.
A6Surf HarpR: Use this on the Search screen
to temporarily increase experience earned.",
  "4.1361.0" => "A6Wind MarimbaR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily increase Rupees gained.
A6Coral TriangleR: Use this on the Search screen
to temporarily increase the amount of Food found.",
  "4.1362.0" => "A6Organ of Evening CalmR: Use on the Search
screen to temporarily increase the Material drop rate.
A6Thunder DrumR: Use this on the Search
screen to temporarily increase the weapon drop rate.",
  "4.1363.0" => "Multi-Element Weapons",
  "4.1364.0" => "A6Multi-element weaponsR are weapons that have
A6an extra elemental attributeR in addition
to their usual attribute.",
  "4.1365.0" => "If that second attribute matches against certain
enemies or in certain scenarios, the battle will be
much easier. However, the second attribute will not
offer bonus effects when attacking.",
  "4.1366.0" => "The Instruments' True Power",
  "4.1367.0" => "Awakening the Wind Fish unlocks the true power of
the Instruments of the Sirens. Siren Power will last
twice as long as usual.",
  "4.1368.0" => "Additionally, you when be able to use the
Instruments of the Sirens anywhere on the map.",
  "4.1369.0" => "Toon Zelda, Spirit Princess of Hyrule",
  "4.1370.0" => "A war between the Spirits of Good and the Demon
King saw evil sealed away. The land then entrusted
to the people, this princess of Hyrule traveled
with the hero to save the world of Spirit Tracks.",
  "4.1371.0" => "The princess's body was taken by those seeking to
resurrect the Demon King, yet her spirit remained.
By inhabiting the armor of a guardian of the Tower
of Spirits, she used her strength to help the hero.",
  "4.1372.0" => "Her massive sword deals fierce blows, and she
can morph into a giant iron ball to deliver piercing
attacks. By unleashing the light of her spirit she
can deal devastation to entire swaths of enemies.",
  "4.1373.0" => "Grand Travels Map",
  "4.1374.0" => "This expansive land consists of two vastly different
environments: a great plain criss-crossed with
railway tracks, and a sprawling ocean that seems
to reach far beyond the horizon.",
  "4.1375.0" => "You can begin your adventure from whichever
area you'd like.",
  "4.1376.0" => "Explore every corner of the two environments
to find the Dark Ruler lurking somewhere on
the map. Defeat him to win the day!",
  "4.1377.0" => "Phantom Hourglass",
  "4.1378.0" => "The A6Phantom HourglassR can be found in the
center of the map. The hourglass protects the land
from a curse cast by two Boss Giant Beasts, but
A6some sand will fall every three battlesR.",
  "4.1379.0" => "If all the sand falls to the bottom half of the
hourglass, the curse will take effect and
A6moving between map squares will
become more difficultR.",
  "4.1380.0" => "You can restore sand to the top half of the
hourglass by defeating Giant Beasts in squares
with the "Final battle!" name. Winning the same
battle multiple times will restore sand each time.",
  "4.1381.0" => "The A6Boss Giant BeastsR can be encountered
in certain "Final battle!" squares throughout the
map. Defeat all Boss Giant Beasts to lift the
curse from the Grand Travels Map once and for all!",
  "4.1382.0" => "Captain Power and Engine Power",
  "4.1383.0" => "Using one of the ship Item Cards will activate a
A6Captain PowerR, while an engine Item
Card will activate an A6Engine PowerR.",
  "4.1384.0" => "Captain and Engine Powers will last for a limited
amount of time. The powers' duration counters
will decrease by one after each battle.",
  "4.1385.0" => "When a counter reaches zero, the power will fade.
Even if the battle you're fighting doesn't exactly
benefit from the current power, the counter will
still decrease, so use the items wisely!",
  "4.1386.0" => "Captain and Engine Powers cannot override
other Captain or Engine Powers. Once the power
takes effect, it will remain in effect until the
duration counter reaches zero.",
  "4.1387.0" => "A6S.S. LinebeckR: Achieve a higher battle rank
for KO count.
A6Iron ShipR: Achieve a better battle rank for
completion time.",
  "4.1388.0" => "A6Golden ShipR: Achieve a higher battle rank
for damage taken.
A6Spirit TrainR: Battle rank C will be enough
to open all routes.",
  "4.1389.0" => "A6Steel TrainR: Adds random "Recommended"
elements to all battles.
A6Golden TrainR: Lifts character restrictions
from all map squares.",
  "4.1390.0" => "Song Stones",
  "4.1391.0" => "If you're on the same map square as a Song
Stone, you will have the opportunity to A6receive
an Item Card of your choosingR.",
  "4.1392.0" => "Song Stones disappear after one use, but will
reappear after a certain number of battles.",
  "4.1393.0" => "Make the most of every Song Stone you come
across to keep your Item Cards fully stocked!",
  "4.1394.0" => "The Linebeck Trading Company",
  "4.1395.0" => "On map squares with the Linebeck Trading Company,
you can A6swap one Item Card for FoodR.",
  "4.1396.0" => "The Linebeck Trading Company disappears from the
square after just a single trade, but will pop up
again after a certain number of battles.",
  "4.1397.0" => "The Linebeck Trading Company will occasionally
hold a A6Two-For-One SaleR. During these
promotions, trading an Item Card will get you
double the usual amount of food in return.",
  "4.1398.0" => "A Two-For-One Sale lasts for the duration of just
a single battle, so be sure to make the most of
the sale and stock up on Food while you can!",
  "4.1399.0" => "Grand Travels Map Item Cards",
  "4.1400.0" => "A6WhirlwindR: Use this on windmills to reveal
hidden stairways.
A6Fishing RodR: Use this while on water
to reel in fish.",
  "4.1401.0" => "A6CannonR: Use this on boulders to reveal
hidden treasure.
A6Railway TrackR: Use this on severed railways
to open the way toward a neighboring map square.",
  "4.1402.0" => "A6Cyclone SlateR: Use this on golden frogs to
reveal hidden enemies.",
  "4.1403.0" => "Ravio, Traveling Merchant",
  "4.1404.0" => "Legend tells of two worlds that intersect. In A Link
Between Worlds, the hero traversed these mirrored
worlds to protect the sacred Triforce. And on this
journey, he was helped by a peculiar merchant...",
  "4.1405.0" => "This merchant tends to look pretty shady, disguised
in a bunny hood like that. Not to mention he moved
into the hero's house and turned it into an item
rental shop... At least the items were useful!",
  "4.1406.0" => "He dips into his own merchandise in battle, using
his giant rental hammer to smash his foes, his Ice
Rod to create blocks of ice, and various items to
create devastating explosions and cyclones.",
  "4.1407.0" => "Yuga, Sorcerer of Lorule",
  "4.1408.0" => "Legend tells of two worlds that intersect. In A Link
Between Worlds, the hero traversed these mirrored
worlds to protect the sacred Triforce. He uncovered
a sorcerer's plot to revive the Demon King.",
  "4.1409.0" => "This sorcerer tirelessly sought things of true beauty
across both worlds. With the unique power to turn
people into paintings, he did just that to the seven
sages' descendants, capturing them one by one.",
  "4.1410.0" => "In battle he hides within a beautiful picture frame
while his illusory attacks blindside enemies. He can
summon a massive spear from the frame to pierce
his enemies' defenses and to wipe the field clean.",
  "4.1411.0" => "Lorule Map",
  "4.1412.0" => "There are two worlds to explore on the
Lorule adventure map.",
  "4.1413.0" => "You can travel freely between these two worlds
by passing through A6fissuresR.",
  "4.1414.0" => "These fissures are hidden all throughout the
Lorule map, and you can A6find them by
investigating via the Search screenR.",
  "4.1415.0" => "After clearing a map square with a fissure on it,
you can use a A6Wall Painting item cardR
on the fissure to go through it.",
  "4.1416.0" => "Journey through both worlds to find and
defeat the Dark Ruler hidden on the map!",
  "4.1417.0" => "Ravio Board",
  "4.1418.0" => "Hey, nice to meet ya! The name's Ravio.
I'm a totally normal, not-suspicious
traveling merchant!",
  "4.1419.0" => "Amazing work out there! Almost like you're a
hero or something! Wait, what? Really?!
You ARE a hero on an adventure to save the
world?! Well, hey, maybe this will help you out!",
  "4.1420.0" => "Nice Power",
  "4.1421.0" => "That thing that just popped up is called a
A6Ravio BoardR. It shows you the active
Nice powers. Don't even ask, I'm gonna tell
you what a Nice Power is either way!",
  "4.1422.0" => "Now, this is some real insider information... But...
Using item cards on this map will cause some
really A6Nice PowersR to take effect across
the entire map!",
  "4.1423.0" => "This means the cards will always do something,
whether you use them on actual search locations
or even just random spots. Pretty useful, right?",
  "4.1424.0" => "And the A6Ravio BoardR is a handy little
thing that lets you see which Nice Powers are
currently active. Just check the eyes. The
icons there will show you which are in effect!",
  "4.1425.0" => "You can have A6up to two types of Nice Powers
active at the same timeR. Activating a third
one will overwrite the previous effects, so
buyer beware!",
  "4.1426.0" => "But don't worry, you can still use item cards while
a Nice Power is active. As long as the item card
has the same Nice Power effect as the one that's
active, the current power won't disappear!",
  "4.1427.0" => "But wait, there's more! I have a special Ravio
offer for you! I call it "Try Before You Buy!"
Basically, what this means for you is...
A6You get a free item card!R",
  "4.1428.0" => "Go, use it, and remember to check that
handsome little Ravio Board to see which
Nice Power activated. That's it for the rundown.
I hope you enjoy using the Ravio Board!",
  "4.1429.0" => "Lorule Map Item Cards",
  "4.1430.0" => "A6Wall PaintingR: Add darkness to recommended
elements. Use on fissures to warp to another world.",
  "4.1431.0" => "A6Tornado RodR: Adds Darkness to recommended
elements. Use on certain tiles to reveal treasure.
A6Sand RodR: Adds Fire to recommended
elements. Use on sand mounds to reveal treasure.",
  "4.1432.0" => "A6Fire RodR: Adds Fire to recommended
elements. Use on ice statutes to reveal enemies.
A6Ice RodR: Adds Water to recommended elements.
Use on fire statues to travel to neighboring square.",
  "4.1433.0" => "A6Baby MaiamaiR: Adds Water to recommended
elements. Give to Mother Maiamai for treasure.
A6BoomerangR: Adds Lightning to recommended
elements. Use on crystals to reveal hidden treasure.",
  "4.1434.0" => "A6Power GloveR: Adds Lightning to recommended
elements. Use on rocks to reveal enemies.
A6BowR: Adds Light to recommended elements.
Use on Beamos to reveal hidden treasure.",
  "4.1435.0" => "A6HookshotR: Adds Light to recommended elements.
Use on a distant target to move toward it.",
  "4.1436.0" => "A6BombsR: Increases Rupees gained. Use on
cracked walls to reveal hidden treasure.
A6HammerR: Increases attack power. Use on
wooden posts to reveal hidden treasure.",
  "4.1437.0" => "A new fairy has come to visit!",
  "4.1438.0" => "While traveling through the original A6Adventure MapR,
you just may come across a new companion Fairy.
Keep an eye out for her on your adventure!",
  "4.1439.0" => "Reserved",
  "4.1440.0" => "Reserved",
  "4.1610.0" => "All right, let's do this thing!",
  "4.1611.0" => "What a pleasure it is to meet you!",
  "4.1612.0" => "Nice to meet you!",
  "4.1613.0" => "Oh, hey! How's it going?",
  "4.1614.0" => "I have a feeling you and I are going to get along just fine.",
  "4.1615.0" => "Ooh! I'm pretty sure you just got stronger.",
  "4.1616.0" => "A fine job you did!",
  "4.1617.0" => "You were amazing!",
  "4.1618.0" => "Great work! Let's eat. I'm starving!",
  "4.1619.0" => "I saw what you did out there. Not bad!",
  "4.1620.0" => "You know, you weren't too bad out there.",
  "4.1621.0" => "I'm sensing a great strength in you.",
  "4.1622.0" => "Good job!",
  "4.1623.0" => "You're going to take me into your next battle, right? Pretty please?",
  "4.1624.0" => "I honestly can't believe you survived that.",
  "4.1625.0" => "Whew! I can't believe we survived that.",
  "4.1626.0" => "I know that must have been difficult, but you made it seem easy!",
  "4.1627.0" => "Quite the challenge, don't you think?",
  "4.1628.0" => "You looked fantastic out there!",
  "4.1629.0" => "At least we made it out in one piece.",
  "4.1630.0" => "That felt...good!",
  "4.1631.0" => "This'll make for a nice memory, don't you think?",
  "4.1632.0" => "You must feel fantastic right now!",
  "4.1633.0" => "That was way too much fun!",
  "4.1634.0" => "You're pretty impressive, did you know that?",
  "4.1635.0" => "Long time, no see!",
  "4.1636.0" => "I've missed you very much.",
  "4.1637.0" => "It's been too long!",
  "4.1638.0" => "Ready for an adventure? Let's do it!",
  "4.1639.0" => "What do you need today?",
  "4.1640.0" => "Whoa... Amazing style!",
  "4.1641.0" => "Absolutely adorable!",
  "4.1642.0" => "Perfect choice!",
  "4.1643.0" => "Whoa! Absolutely gorgeous!",
  "4.1644.0" => "Um...do you think I look all right?",
  "4.1645.0" => "Yes! This is the perfect look for me.",
  "4.1646.0" => "I really adore this look!",
  "4.1647.0" => "I love the way I look in this!",
  "4.1648.0" => "Is this for me? Thank you so much!",
  "4.1649.0" => "I hope you like my new look...",
  "4.1650.0" => "Well? How do I look?",
  "4.1651.0" => "Do you think I look nice? I hope so!",
  "4.1652.0" => "I love it!",
  "4.1653.0" => "I can't wait to go show off this look!",
  "4.1654.0" => "I'll try not to get these clothes dirty.",
  "4.1655.0" => "Oh boy, did I ever pack it away!",
  "4.1656.0" => "Thank you kindly for the delicious meal!",
  "4.1657.0" => "Eating that delicious food has really improved my morale!",
  "4.1658.0" => "My light is burning brighter now!",
  "4.1659.0" => "Is that it?",
  "4.1660.0" => "My stomach is bursting, but I have tons of energy!",
  "4.1661.0" => "I feel like I can do anything!",
  "4.1662.0" => "I am stuffed!",
  "4.1663.0" => "Nap-time first, then a nice, long walk!",
  "4.1664.0" => "Now I can unleash my full potential!",
  "4.1665.0" => "I want something that's been freshly picked.",
  "4.1666.0" => "My throat is parched...",
  "4.1667.0" => "Let's stir things up a bit, hm? I'd like to try something different today!",
  "4.1668.0" => "I need to eat something that'll really fill me up.",
  "4.1669.0" => "Have you caught any nice fish lately? You know the kind I like!",
  "4.1670.0" => "I could probably push myself to work a little
harder, if only I had something warm to drink!",
  "4.1671.0" => "Some juicy fruits or vegetables, please!",
  "4.1672.0" => "You know what I'd love to eat?
Any plants that might help me fly farther!",
  "4.1673.0" => "All this effort has really parched my throat!",
  "4.1674.0" => "I want to take a food with mysterious powers,
then put it in a salad and eat it.",
  "4.1675.0" => "Oh, perfect! It's just what I was craving...",
  "4.1676.0" => "Ah! That was tremendously refreshing.",
  "4.1677.0" => "I've never before eaten anything so delicious!",
  "4.1678.0" => "Thanks for always feeding me so well!",
  "4.1679.0" => "This is exactly what I wanted. How did you know?",
  "4.1680.0" => "Ooh, yum! I'm about to drool all
over myself. Thank you so much!",
  "4.1681.0" => "Ahh, that was quite nice!",
  "4.1682.0" => "That was so tasty! I wouldn't mind having it again some day...",
  "4.1683.0" => "Where can I get more of this delicious food?",
  "4.1684.0" => "You'll get this for me again, right?",
  "4.1685.0" => "What were you thinking? Yuck!",
  "4.1686.0" => "Oof! My tummy hurts...",
  "4.1687.0" => "I don't like things that aren't yummy in my tummy.",
  "4.1688.0" => "I'd rather be out in the wind and sun right now...",
  "4.1689.0" => "Are you trying to tell me something?",
  "4.1690.0" => "Someone lent you their power!
Hmm...I wonder who it was?",
  "4.1691.0" => "Isn't that sweet! Your friends are lending you a hand.",
  "4.1692.0" => "How wonderful! Somebody helped you out.",
  "4.1693.0" => "This'll give you the power you need to keep on fighting!",
  "4.1694.0" => "Looks like someone's trying to help us out.",
  "4.1695.0" => "With this power, the next battle should be a cinch!",
  "4.1696.0" => "I think I just got a little stronger. Thank you kindly!",
  "4.1697.0" => "It must be nice to have so many friends!",
  "4.1698.0" => "You grew stronger thanks to the efforts of your friends!",
  "4.1699.0" => "We can probably accomplish a lot with this.",
  "4.1700.0" => "All right! I'm on fire today, baby.
Time to push it to the limit!",
  "4.1701.0" => "Don't give up, friend. Our dreams will come true someday!",
  "4.1702.0" => "Feeling tired? I've got something to perk you right up!",
  "4.1703.0" => "Each new day brings such wonderful things to discover!",
  "4.1704.0" => "Today's been great, but I bet tomorrow will be even better.",
  "4.1705.0" => "Hey! Take it easy, buddy.",
  "4.1706.0" => "Take a deep breath, and relax.",
  "4.1707.0" => "I wouldn't mind taking a nice, relaxing soak in a fountain...",
  "4.1708.0" => "It's so nice out today. Why don't we just chill out a bit?",
  "4.1709.0" => "Let's just relax. There's no point rushing things...",
  "4.1710.0" => "The weaklings around here aren't
inspiring much confidence, are they.",
  "4.1711.0" => "Is there a stronger enemy around here?",
  "4.1712.0" => "I may be small, but that doesn't mean I can't take down enemies!",
  "4.1713.0" => "Why the long face? You and I are a force to be reckoned with!",
  "4.1714.0" => "You've got nothing to fear with me around.",
  "4.1715.0" => "Whoa! Spinning round and round and round!",
  "4.1716.0" => "Ooh! Do you like spinning too?",
  "4.1717.0" => "Wanna twirl? Here, follow my lead! Whee!",
  "4.1718.0" => "Round and round and round and round!",
  "4.1719.0" => "La la la... Do you like my pirouette?",
  "4.1720.0" => "Hey there! What's up?",
  "4.1721.0" => "Aren't you exhausted? Let's take a little rest.",
  "4.1722.0" => "You're in fine form today!",
  "4.1723.0" => "How are you feeling today?",
  "4.1724.0" => "You've done well today. Bravo.",
  "4.1725.0" => "I really, really want to grow stronger! Grr!",
  "4.1726.0" => "I'd like to be a real hero one of these days...",
  "4.1727.0" => "Could you teach me some of your moves?",
  "4.1728.0" => "Hey, where are you from? I'd like to go there too someday!",
  "4.1729.0" => "I wouldn't mind being a more...likeable fairy.",
  "4.1730.0" => "We. Will. NEVER. Lose!",
  "4.1731.0" => "Maybe you should train a little bit harder? Just a suggestion!",
  "4.1732.0" => "I'm going to give it everything I got! You know, like I always do.",
  "4.1733.0" => "Today is all about training, training, training! Nothing new, right?",
  "4.1734.0" => "Time to plan ahead for the next battle!",
  "4.1735.0" => "I can leave all the fighting up to you, right? Good!",
  "4.1736.0" => "If the situation seems impossible, I recommend a tactical retreat.",
  "4.1737.0" => "Sometimes the best defense is to cut and run!",
  "4.1738.0" => "I don't want to trip you up during the battle,
so I'll just hang back a bit.",
  "4.1739.0" => "I'll have you know, running away is a perfectly reasonable strategy!",
  "4.1740.0" => "Lemme at 'em! Lemme at 'em!",
  "4.1741.0" => "Well, well. What's next on the schedule?",
  "4.1742.0" => "I wonder what kind of adventures we'll get into next!",
  "4.1743.0" => "Let's go on an epic adventure!",
  "4.1744.0" => "I wonder what we'll find on the battlefield this time around...",
  "4.1745.0" => "You're looking pretty happy today!",
  "4.1746.0" => "Can you give me a smile? Just a little one?",
  "4.1747.0" => "I am feeling extremely happy!",
  "4.1748.0" => "I'm so happy you came to visit me!",
  "4.1749.0" => "Can't I fight in the next battle with you?
Being stuck in the bottle is so boring!",
  "4.1750.0" => "I can feel the power flowing right through me. Whoosh!",
  "4.1751.0" => "Such power! I feel like I can do anything!",
  "4.1752.0" => "I feel so strong right now...like there's nothing I can't do!",
  "4.1753.0" => "I'm ready for an adventure!",
  "4.1754.0" => "Ahh! I bet you can hardly recognize me now!",
  "4.1755.0" => "There's still more for me to do out there!",
  "4.1756.0" => "What a lovely rush. I feel so...accomplished!",
  "4.1757.0" => "That was definitely worth the effort!",
  "4.1758.0" => "I feel like I could fly to the moon and back!",
  "4.1759.0" => "This is absolute perfection.",
  "4.1760.0" => "Let's keep on reaching for the stars!",
  "4.1761.0" => "We'll always be friends, won't we?",
  "4.1762.0" => "We're not going to stop until we reach our goal!",
  "4.1763.0" => "I love a fresh start!",
  "4.1764.0" => "A blank slate... How do you wish to proceed?",
  "4.1765.0" => "Thanks for always being there for me.",
  "4.1766.0" => "I got you a little something...",
  "4.1767.0" => "I really hope you like this.",
  "4.1768.0" => "Let me give you one of my treasures!",
  "4.1769.0" => "This is my way of saying thanks...I guess.",
  "4.1770.0" => "Ah, he-hello!
It's... It's nice to meet you!",
  "4.1771.0" => "What a great battle!
I didn't know you were so strong!",
  "4.1772.0" => "Did I help out as much
as you hoped I would?",
  "4.1773.0" => "(Phew, I didn't think we'd make it through alive...)
What? Oh, no, it's nothing! Great battle!",
  "4.1774.0" => "I'm impressed you weren't scared by those enemies!",
  "4.1775.0" => "Long time no see!
Let's take some time to catch up, OK?",
  "4.1776.0" => "Ohh, you really think I can wear this?
Thank you so much!",
  "4.1777.0" => "So, be honest.
How does it look on me?",
  "4.1778.0" => "(Boy, what nice clothes...)
Huh? Oh, um, thank you for the clothes!",
  "4.1779.0" => "Ohh, that was so much food...
But I feel so strong now! ...And full...",
  "4.1780.0" => "I feel like I'm ready for anything after that!",
  "4.1781.0" => "(I hope I get to eat some sparkling fruit soon...)
Ah, not to sound picky or anything!",
  "4.1783.0" => "Ahh, so delicious! Good food always makes me happy!",
  "4.1784.0" => "Huh? I'm smiling a lot? Well, I guess
it's because this is my favorite food!",
  "4.1785.0" => "(Hrk...) Um... I'm sorry...
But this just doesn't taste very good...",
  "4.1786.0" => "I feel like I can do anything as
long as you're all on my side!",
  "4.1787.0" => "It must be nice having so many friends to help you out.
I bet they make you feel invincible!",
  "4.1788.0" => "For once, I feel like it's going to be a good day.
Let's make sure it is!",
  "4.1789.0" => "Hey, no need to rush into things.
It's important to understand the situation before moving out.",
  "4.1790.0" => "No fear! No hesitation! No regrets!
Go, go, go! We can do it!",
  "4.1791.0" => "Round and round and round! Ahh, I could do this all day...
(Hrk... Went around a few too many times...!)",
  "4.1792.0" => "Hey, how's it going?
Be careful out there, OK?",
  "4.1793.0" => "I may be small enough to fit in a bottle...
But if you just let me out, I promise I'll be able to help you!",
  "4.1794.0" => "Must...train...harder...!
I can do it! Let me at 'em!",
  "4.1795.0" => "Ah, I'm... I'm not sure I can fight through these nerves...
But I'll do my best...!",
  "4.1796.0" => "Ohh, what does the next battle hold for us?
The suspense is killing me!",
  "4.1797.0" => "I can't stop smiling.
I'm just in a good mood!",
  "4.1798.0" => "Hey, I got stronger!
All right! Let's go get 'em!",
  "4.1799.0" => "Oh, wow... I wouldn't have gotten this far without you!
Thank you so much!",
  "4.1800.0" => "I think I can do so much more than before...
If only you help me out again!",
  "4.1801.0" => "Um... It's not much, but...I want you to have this.",
  "4.1802.0" => "Hi there! I have a feeling we're gonna have
a lot of fun together!",
  "4.1803.0" => "Hey, you're not too bad out there!",
  "4.1804.0" => "You really went all out during that battle!
Was it because you heard me cheering for you?",
  "4.1805.0" => "Phew, that was a tough battle... But I believed in
you every step of the way!",
  "4.1806.0" => "Simply a-ma-zing! I think all these battles
are making you stronger!",
  "4.1807.0" => "Hey, long time no see!
Let's play a game together!",
  "4.1808.0" => "Hey, check it out! It kinda suits me,
don't you think?",
  "4.1809.0" => "Ohh, I really like these clothes!
I'm excited to wear them out and about!",
  "4.1810.0" => "So, what do you think? I look like
a real hero now, don't I?",
  "4.1811.0" => "Ha, I picked up some new skills! But don't be
trying to copy my moves, OK?",
  "4.1812.0" => "Oof, I think I may have eaten a bit too much...
I'd better do some laps to burn that off!",
  "4.1813.0" => "I'm in the mood for something that's tasty,
yet not quite ripe...",
  "4.1814.0" => "Is it weird that I'm in the mood for something that
has whiskers...? Or should I say it's fishy?",
  "4.1815.0" => "Ohh, did you know this was my favorite food?
Consider me wholly satisfied after that meal!",
  "4.1816.0" => "It's always easy to eat a whole bunch of your
favorite food, don't you think?",
  "4.1817.0" => "Maybe next time I could have something...
I don't know... Just...different?",
  "4.1818.0" => "Having friends by your side means you can push
yourself harder than usual!",
  "4.1819.0" => "I can feel how powerful everyone else is!
Let's pool that strength and charge forward!",
  "4.1820.0" => "Ohh, my heart's all aflutter just thinking about
all the things I'm gonna do!",
  "4.1821.0" => "Sometimes it's a good idea to take a look around
first and check out what's going on.",
  "4.1822.0" => "It doesn't matter what kind of enemy they can
drum up next. There's no stopping us!",
  "4.1823.0" => "Ohh-ho... Dum de dum, dum de dum...!",
  "4.1824.0" => "Hey, don't forget me!
Where are we going today, anyway?",
  "4.1825.0" => "I'll get even stronger, and then I'll
become the true hero!",
  "4.1826.0" => "Boom! Haha! We've got another no-holds-barred
day ahead of us, right?!",
  "4.1827.0" => "H-hey, a tactical retreat never hurt anyone, right?
There's more to life than fighting...!",
  "4.1828.0" => "Let's not dillydally!
Keep moving forward!",
  "4.1829.0" => "Let's play a game together!
I'm just in such a good mood!",
  "4.1830.0" => "Ahh, what a morale boost! I feel like I could
accomplish anything I put my mind to!",
  "4.1831.0" => "This power coursing through my body...!
I don't think I can keep still!",
  "4.1832.0" => "Ahh, I feel like I'm born again!",
  "4.1833.0" => "Here, I want you to have this.
Tell me a story in return?",
  "4.1835.0" => "I will gladly fight by your side.",
  "4.1836.0" => "That fight was rather difficult, but I think
it went rather well. Wouldn't you agree?",
  "4.1837.0" => "You sure are the dependable sort!",
  "4.1838.0" => "It's good to see you don't betray others'
expectations of you.",
  "4.1839.0" => "There's an incredible power to you.
Perhaps even more than meets the eye...",
  "4.1840.0" => "I'm glad we have the chance to fight together again.",
  "4.1841.0" => "In a word, this new look is...
Perfect.",
  "4.1842.0" => "Yes, I think this will work.",
  "4.1843.0" => "These aren't exactly clothes fit for fighting...
But... Well, thank you anyway.",
  "4.1844.0" => "You've come a long way, but don't forget
what it was like just starting out.",
  "4.1845.0" => "You can depend on me more from here on!",
  "4.1846.0" => "I actually get a lot of power from foods humans can't eat.",
  "4.1847.0" => "Give me something filling that will prepare me for battle.",
  "4.1848.0" => "Ahh... You really understand me, huh?",
  "4.1849.0" => "I thank you for your small kindness.",
  "4.1850.0" => "This is not what I was hoping for...",
  "4.1851.0" => "You have my thanks, battle friends.",
  "4.1852.0" => "Looks like I have plenty of support.",
  "4.1853.0" => "Every nighttime ends, sooner or later.
Let's keep our spirits up and keep moving forward!",
  "4.1854.0" => "I will soothe your wounds and provide comfort.
Close your eyes and relax...",
  "4.1855.0" => "We won't lose. Not with me on your side!",
  "4.1856.0" => "Around, and around, and around...
And around we go!",
  "4.1857.0" => "Hey, don't be too hard on yourself.
I think you're doing a great job!",
  "4.1858.0" => "What is it that you aspire to?",
  "4.1859.0" => "I'm looking forward to seeing your true strength.",
  "4.1860.0" => "Hm... I suppose retreating is one
type of strategy...",
  "4.1861.0" => "I'm honored I could lend my skills to you in battle.",
  "4.1862.0" => "I'm sure the goddesses will smile down on us today.",
  "4.1863.0" => "I think I can finally show you my true strength.",
  "4.1864.0" => "At last... This is my reward for all the battles and training!",
  "4.1865.0" => "I need to dedicate myself even more to my growth.",
  "4.1866.0" => "Think wisely before using this.",
  "5.200.0" => "Set difficulty level.",
  "5.201.0" => "Turn automatic network connection on or off.",
  "5.202.0" => "Select controllers.",
  "5.203.0" => "Adjust control options.",
  "5.204.0" => "Set volume for music and sound effects.",
  "5.205.0" => "Select controller for Player 1.",
  "5.206.0" => "Select controller for Player 2.",
  "5.207.0" => "Change Player 1 settings.",
  "5.208.0" => "Change Player 2 settings.",
  "5.209.0" => "Turn controller rumble on or off.",
  "5.210.0" => "Adjust horizontal PK camera setting.",
  "5.211.0" => "Adjust vertical PK camera setting.",
  "5.212.0" => "Select button configuration.",
  "5.213.0" => "Adjust music volume.",
  "5.214.0" => "Adjust sound effect volume. ",
